-- Add quest_offer_reward rows present in the upstream LegionCore 2024-10-23 world dump
-- (The-Legion-Preservation-Project/LegionCore-7.3.5) but missing from our world DB.
-- Reward-screen text/emotes for these quest IDs were previously blank in game.
INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES (2986,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.$B$BYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.',0),(5634,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m glad you\'ve arrived, $N. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light. There are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we\'ll begin discussing some of those now.',0),(5635,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m glad you\'ve arrived, $N. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.$B$BThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we\'ll begin discussing some of those now.',0),(5636,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks for the done work!',0),(5637,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m glad you\'ve arrived, $N. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.$B$BThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we\'ll begin discussing some of those now.',0),(5638,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks for the done work!',0),(5639,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m glad you\'ve arrived, $N. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.$B$BThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we\'ll begin discussing some of those now.',0),(5653,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks for the done work!',0),(7493,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A dragon slayer and a seasoned leatherworker? You do not cease to astonish, hero. I am humbled.$B$BPlease accept what I am about to teach you. This knowledge will prove to be invaluable if you are to destroy what remains of the Black Dragonflight.$B$BCreate the cloak from the scales of the brood mother. It will protect you and your allies against the incendiary breath of the Lord of Blackrock... Nefarian.',0),(7497,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A dragon slayer and a seasoned leatherworker? You do not cease to astonish, hero. I am humbled.$B$BPlease accept what I am about to teach you. This knowledge will prove to be invaluable if you are to destroy what remains of the Black Dragonflight.$B$BCreate the cloak from the scales of the brood mother. It will protect you and your allies against the incendiary breath of the Lord of Blackrock... Nefarian.',0),(7704,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is better than even I could have thought possible! The Chambermaid\'s magical pillow is mine! You better believe you\'re going to get a nice reward for this accomplishment, $n!',0),(8329,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome to the Sunspire, young $C! Mastery of weapons and battle tactics begins here and now - all I ask of my pupils is that they cover payment for training costs that may come up, and that they are as good of a listener as they are an aspiring $C. The lessons I have to teach are extensive, and I don\'t like to repeat myself unnecessarially.$B$BLet\'s get to it then!',0),(8579,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see that you\'re no ordinary mortal, $n. Your chances against the Old God, however infinitely small, are greater than ours at this point. After all, while he expects dragons at his doorstep, he is not prepared for someone like you.$B$BJust as Anachronos and Staghelm defeated the Qiraji a thousand years ago through the alliance of mortal and dragon races, we too shall form a pact. Gain the trust of the Bronze Dragonflight and you\'ll gain our trust. Only then we shall make a true champion out of you.',0),(8621,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $n. You\'ve proven you\'re no ordinary mortal.$B$BI give you these with the confidence they\'ll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.',0),(8622,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I did not expect you to return from your attempt, $n.$B$BYou\'ve fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.$B$BBy slaying C\'Thun you\'ve not only saved all of Azeroth, you\'ve also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.$B$BAccept this breastplate as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.$B$BMay its power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!',0),(8623,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.$B$BTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.',0),(8624,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes... the worm\'s skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we\'ve destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!',0),(8631,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes... the worm\'s skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we\'ve destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!',0),(8640,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes... the worm\'s skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we\'ve destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!',0),(8658,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes... the worm\'s skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we\'ve destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!',0),(8661,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I did not expect you to return from your attempt, $n.$B$BYou\'ve fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.$B$BBy slaying C\'Thun you\'ve not only saved all of Azeroth, you\'ve also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.$B$BAccept these robes as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.$B$BMay their power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!',0),(8745,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Greetings, champion. I am Jonathan, keeper of the sacred gong and eternal watcher of the Bronze Flight.$B$BI have been empowered by the Timeless One himself to grant you an item of your choosing from his timeless treasure trove. May it aid you in your battles against C\'Thun.',0),(8747,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.$B$BThe signet ring of the defender will offer superior protection against the forces of evil.$B$BBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.',0),(8752,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.$B$BThe signet ring of the conqueror will greatly enhance your physical attacks.$B$BBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.',0),(8757,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.$B$BThe signet ring of the invoker will greatly enhance your magical and natural abilities.$B$BBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.',0),(8763,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The machine lets off a little rumble and a small amount of steam as it starts working. It is not too long thereafter until it stops, heralded by another small jet of steam erupting from it. A door hatch opens, revealing a batch of preserved holly!',0),(8799,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The machine lets off a little rumble and a small amount of steam as it starts working. It is not too long thereafter until it stops, heralded by another small jet of steam erupting from it. A door hatch opens, revealing a batch of preserved holly!',0),(9177,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Sylvanas takes the necklace from your grasp.>$B$BIt can\'t be! After all this time, I thought it was lost forever.$B$B<After a lingering moment the Lady seems to become aware once again of her surroundings, composing herself.>$B$BYou thought this would amuse me? Do you think I long for a time before I was the queen of the Forsaken? Like you, it means nothing to me, and Alleria Windrunner is a long dead memory!$B$B<She drops the amulet to the ground.>$B$BYou may now remove yourself from my presence, $C.',0),(10379,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah. good, another has arrived. Time may not matter to me, but to you it is of the essence. There is much for you to learn and there is much I wish to teach you. You simply must prove your worth. Do that, and you shall be greatly rewarded.',0),(11997,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',21232),(12103,1,603,0,0,0,1500,0,0,'С возвращением в земли живых, $n. Мы чуть не потеряли тебя при взрыве! К счастью для нас, поблизости оказался Скитающийся остров.$b$bМестные жители любезно согласились принять нас в своем храме. Конечно, это не Пик Безмятежности, но это место станет нам хорошим домом.',21491),(13022,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, $n, and offer you this token...',0),(13023,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, $n, and offer you this token...',0),(13065,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, $n, and offer you this token...',0),(13066,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, $n, and offer you this token...',0),(13067,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, $n, and offer you this token...',0),(13429,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Xi\'ri pulses with energy as you feel an object materialize in your hands. It is the medallion you gave to A\'dal on Akama\'s behalf, its power augmented by the naaru\'s magic. The Sha\'tar have entrusted you with the Medallion of Karabor, and with it access to the Black Temple.>',0),(13504,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work. Thank you, $C.',0),(13505,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Perfect! Thank you so much. I would hate to lose more records of our culture to war - far too much has been sacrificed already.',0),(13506,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\"Another?\" They have more than one. I will not leave any of my people to be tortured, we must act quickly.',0),(13507,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work. One more threat we can worry a bit less about. We\'ll continue the offensive while they are still off-guard.',0),(13508,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Alanndarian looks very pale, though shallow breaths betray the life that remains in her.>$B$BYou\'re here... to save me? A bit later... than I hoped.',0),(13509,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work. That should slow them down a bit.',0),(13510,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Some sort of shield you say? We might have a way around that. Balthule had an idea for breaking whatever protective enchantments their shaman had, so it might work on this too. Thank you for saving Aynasha and bringing me this information - it may well make the difference in our battle.',0),(13511,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Alanndarian is dead then. That saddens me greatly, but it is not entirely unexpected. I expect no mercy from these savages, and will show them none.',0),(13512,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve shown a great deal of talent for one so young. Good work. It seems the final battle is before us.',0),(13513,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These will do perfectly. I will prepare them for Sandrya - you are sure to be dispatched to meet with her shortly.',0),(13514,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You performed excellently up there! We are fortunate to have you with us.$B$BI haven\'t yet received word regarding their leader. If you haven\'t spoken with Sandrya at the cave in the back of the vale, be sure to do so before you depart.',0),(13515,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We owe a great debt to you for all that you\'ve done to see this battle through.$B$BNot often can we claim victories so decisively, but it seems there\'s far more to this plot than just the Shatterspear. If you haven\'t already checked his body for information, make sure to do so before you leave.',0),(13519,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $n. The Twilight\'s Hammer is a dangerous cult. It would be foolish to underestimate the danger they represent.',0),(13520,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This will do perfectly. Thank you so much!$B$BI suspect they will want to thank you personally should they recover, so perhaps you can stop by later on.',0),(13521,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The machine crackles loudly, and then Wizbang\'s static-ridden voice becomes audible.>$B$BLovely! I hope you didn\'t kill too many of them. We\'re not trying to wipe out the population, we just need to get to the source of this corruption quickly! I\'m proceeding with the analysis now.',0),(13522,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your efforts are very much appreciated. Since the Cataclysm, the elementals have been out of control. We have little hope of taking back Auberdine without extinguishing their presence first.',0),(13523,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve succeeded... it hasn\'t all been in vain...$B$BMy time approaches. Go now, $n, and may Elune protect you.',0),(13525,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why have you come here, outsider?$B$B<You tell the elder that you were sent by Foriel Broadleaf at the Grove of the Ancients. He seems to relax slightly.>$B$BThe elf is right. The forces of Felwood have seeped into Darkshore and sickened my people.',0),(13526,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are poor, weak stalks, but they are all we have. The corruption spreads quickly, even among the plants of the forest.',0),(13527,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This definitely looks like the stuff they were eating. Let me take a closer peek...',0),(13528,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Static precedes Wizbang\'s distorted voice.>$B$BThe results are coming in now. We should have some information on how the bears contracted this in just a moment.',0),(13529,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is done then. Thank you. I only hope that the wildlife here will see more peace with his passing.',0),(13537,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It looks like fishing\'s your thing. My belly appreciates the gift.$B$BI\'m thinking you would get more use out of this pole than I would. Have at it.',0),(13544,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Elder Brolg accepts the blessed bundle from you and looks over it.>$B$BThis is exactly what we needed. The bear\'s spirit favors us and there may be hope for my brothers after all.',0),(13545,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have done well. My people have begun to emerge from their madness, but they will fall back into it if we do not deal with the source of the corruption.',0),(13546,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. You are a hero to my people. Without you, we would be doomed to madness and death. May the bear spirit always watch over you.',0),(13554,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This should be plenty! Thanks so much! I\'ll get working on a cure for this nastiness immediately.',0),(13557,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am pleased to hear that you were able to free some of the remaining wildlife. With a bit of good fortune, we will find the cure for the corruption that the others have faced before any more of them die.',0),(13560,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The decoys worked then? Great to hear it! Don\'t you worry yourself one bit about the treasures. Me and Gary will take care of the rest this time around.$B$BTruth be told, if something went wrong again and I lost any more of you adventurer types, I\'m pretty sure they\'d kick me out of town.',0),(13561,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have my thanks. Though they may not be able to show it, you have the thanks of the Highborne spirits as well.$B$BFare safely, traveler.',0),(13562,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have our thanks. It is time that we leave the past behind us, and start looking to our future.',0),(13563,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. Perhaps it would have been better... if I had done it myself. But even after these thousands of years, I could not bear to raise my hand against my beloved.$B$BPlease, I would be alone with my grief...',0),(13564,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Greetings, traveler. You seem to have an interest in my friend here. You\'re here on behalf of his friend Volcor then I imagine? If Volcor didn\'t come himself, he must be injured as well. I hope he recovers quickly.$B$BGimclaw is too injured to be moved far and he\'s going to need some immediate treatment. I\'m afraid I can\'t let you take him back just yet, but perhaps you can help me while I tend to him.',0),(13565,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, ally. We shall keep a more vigilant eye should they return.',0),(13566,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These will do perfectly. These are the final ingredients for an incense I\'ve been working on. I will explain in just a moment, let me mix these in first.',0),(13567,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am the caretaker for my kind, leading not through force, but through wisdom and swift action. Wisdom is what carries us into the deeper forest when danger beckons and swiftness is what leaves our enemies basking in our absence.$B$BIn this wisdom, I see through to your true intentions, and I know that you are deserving of my blessing, the blessing of my swiftness. It can be yours, but know that the other spirits will not welcome you once you proceed - consider this carefully before accepting my boon.',0),(13568,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I share these forests willingly, accepting night elf kind into my home, and on occasion calling them friend. Though they have been tainted greatly in recent memory, I can see in you the same strength, honor, and spirit that first endeared them to me.$B$BIf you place value in the ferocity necessary to overcome all odds, then I am willing to call you my champion. Know now that if you side with my kind, the other spirits will not accept you, so consider your choice carefully.',0),(13569,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So it is done. You have received the blessing of a great animal spirit, and I shall now complete the ritual for you. Please stand still.',0),(13570,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I just want to offer my sincerest thanks for all that you\'ve done for us. In my grief, I\'m afraid that I didn\'t extend the gratitude that you truly deserve. We may not have made it here without you.$B$BKnow that you will always have friends here.$B$BAnd you needn\'t worry about my loneliness. Grimclaw has taken to keeping me company, and I have to say he\'s a more comforting companion than I would have expected.$B$BTake this, and go with all our blessings. Until we meet again, $n.',0),(13572,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. With your efforts, we might be able to save the Blackwood who remain.',0),(13578,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $R. Soon my kin will rest.',0),(13582,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Aroom lets out a long low-pitched hoot.>$B$BFinally kin may rest.',0),(13589,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Glynda sent you to lend a hand, did she? I\'m glad she did - I could certainly use the help.$B$BI\'m working on our initial plans to start whittling away at their ranks. Please feel free to help Tysha and Balthule in the meantime.',0),(13590,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good to meet you. Word has been sent to me of the efforts you have made to aid us against the trolls, and I must admit I am a bit impressed. The final fight is upon us now, I hope you are prepared.',0),(13591,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well, this news is disturbing indeed. I will start dispatching messengers to Ashenvale immediately and see if we can\'t get some reinforcements prepared for them.$B$BI cannot thank you enough for all the help you\'ve lent us in these trying times. Such heroic deeds deserve reward. I think I might have something that will serve you perfectly.',0),(13596,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent job, $n. Now give me a moment to examine the plans you\'ve brought me.',0),(13597,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'For countless ages I have walked these forests and lived in these mountains. Through snow and fire, I have watched civilizations crumble and nature press on. Now, the very earth turns against us, and it becomes very apparent that we must fight if our legacy is to continue.$B$BYour heart is true, and I would choose you as our champion. If you value the thick hide and resilience of my kind, then accept my boon. Know that the other spirits will not accept you once this choice is made, so choose wisely.',0),(13598,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have my thanks, young one. We should be able to speed Grimclaw\'s recovery dramatically with this salve.',0),(13599,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve returned! It is good to see you again. I suppose we have you to thank for Grimclaw\'s return?$B$BI\'m afraid... I have some bad news. I\'ve been unable to purge the toxin... their conditions worsen. Gershalla died shortly after you left, and Volcor... Volcor passed just before you came back.$B$BHe lived long enough to see Grimclaw come back safely, so he died with a smile on his face. I\'m just sorry that I couldn\'t do more.$B$BFor now, I\'m doing everything I can to save Shaldyn, so please excuse me.',0),(13601,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you for coming to our assistance. As you can see, the refugees\' situation is dire.',0),(13612,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $C!$B$BYour efforts will help keep the enemy on their heels while our forces sweep across the land!',0),(13613,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $R. I shall include your service to the Horde in my report.$B$BI should have these troops fit to fight again in no time!',0),(13615,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C.$B$BThis should help get us by until our shipment arrives.',0),(13618,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Listen carefully, $R....',0),(13619,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Kadrak listens intently as you share Gorat\'s last words.>$B$BIt is as I feared, then. May his rest be peaceful - only not yet!',0),(13620,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let\'s have a look, $C.',0),(13621,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $R.$B$BThe elf captain is dead and the soul of one of our beloved brethren can sleep in peace.$B$BI shall pass on word of your deeds to my superiors in Orgrimmar.',0),(13622,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Analyzing fragments... please stand by.',0),(13628,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, $C. It is good to see that the road to Mor\'shan Ramparts remains clear.',0),(13629,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Object integrity confirmed. Please hold while solidified residue is removed.',0),(13635,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The South Gate status report? Excellent. I\'ve been awaiting news from them for a while.$B$BWith the increasing number of troggs in the hills on all sides, I fear the outposts will be the first to feel any aggressive action.',0),(13636,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Orders! Let\'s see what we have here... hah! He wants me to deal with the infestation of rat men. We\'re already in the middle of that, so no real deviation there.$B$BCare to lend a hand?',0),(13640,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It seems you\'ve solved one problem only to face another, $C.',0),(13651,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you for the oil, $C. Now prepare yourself!$B$BMy runner has returned with some desperate news....$B$BSplintertree is surrounded!',0),(13653,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Gorka...$B$BWe must always be prepared for losses. Her honorable service to the Horde will not be forgotten.$B$BAnd her sacrifice shall not be in vain!',0),(13657,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Our historical records! The thought of dark iron vermin delving into our past just made me sick to my stomach.$B$BWe appreciate you bringing this back to us. We\'d like to offer you some coin as a reward.',0),(13658,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ug, I can\'t believe they got their hands on our transport routes - that was just asking for trouble!!$B$BThank you for getting this back to us before they were able to do much with it! You probably saved us a lot of heartache. Please accept some coin as a reward for your efforts.',0),(13659,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah! Think they got a kick out of seeing how low they were on our list of threat assessments! This document was admittedly a bit out of date, but none the less amusing.$B$BOf course, we\'ll offer you some money as a reward for returning this anyway - your efforts are appreciated!',0),(13660,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Our artifact records! I was pretty well worried what the dark irons might try to steal with this information at their disposal.$B$BThank you for bringing this back to us. We\'ll gladly part with some coin to express our gratitude.',0),(13661,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You located all of our documents! We can\'t thank you enough for the help... we\'d all but given up hope. It seemed sure that the dark irons would be able to act upon all of this information soon. It\'s good to know that they\'ll be left blind in their attacks for quite a while yet.$B$BTo thank you for all of your efforts on our behalf, we would like to offer you a gift. An artifact really... something we recovered from one of our digs. You have the appreciation of all of the Explorers\' League.',0),(13712,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Gorka\'s death was not in vain, $n.$B$BSplintertree would have certainly fallen if we hadn\'t come when we did.$B$BNow we must get to work shoring up her defenses.$B$BThis isn\'t over....',0),(13730,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, yes!$B$BThis will teach those elves, just you watch!',0),(13751,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What\'s this? Who are you!?$B$B<Durak reads Draaka\'s note.>$B$BHrmphh...$B$BDraaka should know better than to be so brazen, but it looks like you\'re up to your eyes in this with as much to lose as anyone.$B$BVery well.',0),(13797,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done! These should hold a curse long enough for our purposes....',0),(13798,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Did you feel it, $n!?$B$BThe raw fel power seething through your being?$B$BThere is nothing else like it!',0),(13801,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Woohooo!!$B$BYou\'ve silenced the voices! Thank you, thank you!',0),(13803,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Tainting the Forest\'s Heart?$B$BHow ruthless - an utterly vicious blow....$B$BI adore the idea!',0),(13805,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is done?$B$BGood work, $n. That will gradually weaken their forces, as well as their spirit.',0),(13806,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $R.$B$BOne less thing we have to worry about!',0),(13808,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have your work cut out for you here, friend.$B$BLet\'s hope that you\'re up to the task,,,,',0),(13815,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, $n.$B$BYou\'ve demoralized the enemy and harvested resources for the Horde.$B$BLet\'s hope the rest of the mission goes as well.',0),(13825,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey, I remember you! Aren\'t you the $C that helped me make all that clamlette back in the day?$B$BTell you what, step on up and I\'ll show you my newest recipe - it\'s simple and delicious!',0),(13831,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Tharnariun Treetender pages through the notes as you relate your story, the lines in his face deepening with concern.>$B$BSo the Forsaken have been studying Foulhoof\'s work? My gut crawls at the thought of what they might have done were they able to weaponize his corruption. You\'ve done well to destroy their work, but this raises deeper concerns. What brought the Forsaken to our doorstep? Are they working with the Shatterspear trolls to our north? Sorrows are heaping upon sorrows, $C. I\'m glad you\'re here.',0),(13841,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fools!!$B$BThis Draaka woman has allowed herself to be manipulated by a demon!$B$B<Garrosh studies you for a moment.>$B$BAnd I smell its taint on you as well, $C....',0),(13842,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Grah... very well.$B$BI\'ll remove the bounty I had placed upon your head. Though I am sorely tempted to end your life anyway, just on principle.$B$BBe sure that you never raise my ire again, $n. Now, get out of my sight...',0),(13843,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You take note of the information displayed in the schematic and the materials required to construct the scrapbot kit.',0),(13844,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let\'s see what we\'ve got here.... By Elune, his notes are scrawled in a half dozen languages. What is this, blood? This archive makes my flesh seethe, but at least it\'s secure. It will take us some time to decipher these notes.$B$BOh - your reward? Yes, here. Nice work with those undead scavengers. Now get back to the fight.',0),(13848,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Commander Grimfang\'s brow wrinkles as he reads the report.>$B$BThis is grim news, indeed.$B$BMay the spirits preserve them until we can fight our way to Splintertree....',0),(13865,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C.$B$BThey\'re in complete disarray. Just look at them!',0),(13866,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are just in time, $C. Old Kulg has been slinking around those woods too long. He grows too cautious, jumping at shadows. We will fear this forest no longer - the time has come to subdue Ashenvale once and for all!',0),(13870,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Gorthak sighs disappointedly.>$B$BIf only you\'d arrived an hour ago....$B$BThe diplomat suffered mortal wounds at the hands of an elf assassin.$B$BHow the enemy was able to infiltrate the camp undetected remains a mystery.',0),(13871,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C.$B$BOne last request - it would probably be best if none of my laborers knew this assassin ever existed.',0),(13873,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Gurtar listens as you inform him of Sheelah\'s passing.>$B$BI\'ll deliver this to Hellscream personally, $R.$B$BIn the meantime, there\'s something I need you to do for me....',0),(13875,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Recognizing at once the nature of the gift, Draaka begins to weep.>$B$BOh, $n. Thank you for this gift! It means more than you could know.$B$BHe hasn\'t forgotten...',0),(13878,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You save the wolves! So brave! Someday, maybe you get a wolf just like that to ride.$B$B<Dorak looks at the burning stables, then at the nearby river.>$B$BWhat should I do now?',0),(13879,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The goblin stares at you and blinks several times before speaking.>$B$BThe spirits whispered that help would soon arrive.$B$BPardon my surprise, but I was hoping the spirits would guide someone a little more... heroic.$B$BThese elementals are trusted allies. Listen to them and do their bidding. If we fail, there will remain nothing in Ashenvale worth fighting for.',0),(13881,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Kathrena recoils at your description of the ravaged animals and the cruel device at the bottom of the lake>$B$B$n, this is terrible. What is that thing, and how did it get there? Something is devouring these animals, physically and spiritually. I had suspected the satyrs or some sort of disease was the culprit, but this is shaping up to be something ... unnatural.',0),(13882,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Perfect, this is everything. Did you have fun collecting the wisp? I used to chase the wisps around Ashenvale when I was just a girl.$B$B<Lost in memories for a moment, Kathrena suddenly grows somber.>$B$BI\'m afraid I\'ve found out what we\'re dealing with.',0),(13883,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $R.$B$BI\'ll show them how an armored ship should be built!',0),(13885,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So the animals are safe, then. Thank you, thank you!$B$BBut now it\'s time to turn our attention to the source.',0),(13888,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done it! The spirits were right after all!$B$BThe power of fire is subdued and the four elements are returned to harmony.$B$BThe rest of Ashenvale is spared this fiery fate. You have the eternal thanks of the Earthen Ring.',0),(13890,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, $R!$B$BNo more ships will run aground, thanks to you.',0),(13891,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Love of Elune, look at you. That must\'ve been some fight! You\'re covered in what looks like... chowder.$B$BIf a mere minion could cause so much agony here in Darkshore, I can\'t even imagine the suffering that a true Old One could bring about.$B$BWell, at least the animals are safe for now. I will plant the sapling you created to help rebuild this shattered land. Thank you, $n! I\'d give you a hug but, you know. Chowder.',0),(13892,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is dire news, $n. If you are correct, then we\'d best act swiftly and decisively.$B$BWe cannot allow this \"Soggoth\" to be brought back to life.',0),(13893,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The dwarf\'s story is unsettling... yet informative. It seems we have few options left.',0),(13895,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Aros\'s body appears to be lifeless yet still warm. Perhaps his killers are nearby.',0),(13896,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, we know a thing or two about this Soggoth. The question is... do you really want to know?',0),(13897,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We can finally rest here now, $n. It appears Darkshore has been saved -- and we have you to thank for it.',0),(13898,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. The naga seek the destruction and subjugation of all surface-dwellers -- do not hesitate to drive them out of our lands and back into the shadowy ocean depths where they belong.',0),(13899,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The walord doesn\'t seem to have the horn on him. Perhaps he was telling the truth.',0),(13900,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $n. Unfortunately the battle is far from over.',0),(13901,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent!$B$BLet the naga retreat back into the seas where they belong!',0),(13907,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Bravo, $n! Now let\'s take a look-see at our new situation.$B$BWhat? MORE murlocs? I swear on my stones, the more murlocs you kill, the more murlocs appear. Is it just me? We\'re going to need a new approach.',0),(13909,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Archaeologist Groff picks through the wreckage.>$B$BWell, not much here that don\'t look stepped on, sat on, or soaked in a toilet. But toss some thatch on top and it\'ll do.$B$BTell me, $n, do you consider yourself an architect?',0),(13910,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Har har, that sounds like quite a heap you built there. Did they take to it? Good, good! Let\'s see if my plan comes to fruition.$B$B<Archaeologist Groff watches as scores of murlocs stream down the beach, pouring into the hovel from all corners of the compass. Gradually his brows knit together.>$B$BWhat have I done?',0),(13911,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, you\'ve helped the Prospector find his missing journal! To think it was here all along.$B$BSomeday you\'ll have to show me this other set of ruins he\'s always going on about.',0),(13912,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Spectacular! Good work, $n. I\'m sure Remtravel would thank you himself if he could remember your name.$B$BLook at the surface of the disc - these microscopic etchings - this is amazing. I\'m certain this strange wheel holds information, if only we could read it...',0),(13918,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why yes, yes, this is it! See here, the slot is the exact dimensions of the ancient disc, just as I\'d surmised. Here\'s your reward, $n - you\'ve earned it.$B$B$B$BAre you ready to meet history face to face? Let\'s see what the ancients have to say!',0),(13920,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These venison should make our soldiers\' spirits rise for the coming battles. Here\'s something for your troubles.',0),(13923,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You come here as a child, $R.$B$BYou shall leave here a battle-hardened $C of the Horde!$B$BThat, or a corpse....',0),(13925,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Interesting ... It sounds like our cure will keep the wildlife safe, but you say you saw something else? Some kind of angry presence?\r\n\r\nThis is a good sign, $n. Whatever is behind this isn\'t happy, and that means we\'re on to something. ',0),(13936,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let me tell ya somethin\' $C!$B$BThe bossman simply doesn\'t appreciate the art and craftsmanship that goes into making fine explosives.',0),(13942,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is PERFECT!$B$BOh, just wait \'til you see what I can do with this....',0),(13943,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $R. But there is much that remains to be done here.',0),(13944,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So, Tweedle found a way to get those explosives working, eh?$B$BIt\'s about time...',0),(13947,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your deeds today shall live long in the Horde\'s glorious history.$B$BYour efforts have dealt a devastating blow to the enemy!',0),(13948,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is dire news, $n. If you are correct, then we\'d best act swiftly and decisively.$B$BWe cannot allow this \"Soggoth\" to be brought back to life.',0),(13949,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re a sight, $R. That\'s the first caravan to make it through this week!',0),(13952,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(13953,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The naga are in league with the Twilight\'s Hammer? Just what we needed.',0),(13958,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Thagg listens intently as you recount your assault on Astranaar.>$B$BThis is good news indeed, $R. But right now, we need more than just good news here.$B$BThese triage kits will be put to good use!',0),(13961,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh my. We want to question this Quilboar, not tenderize him!',0),(13962,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very well, $n.$B$BYou have succeeded where I could not. You have earned my respect.',0),(13963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very interesting - our brute here seems both enthralled and terrified of the one they call \"Tortusk.\" A powerful leader can inspire his people to acts of greatness or atrocity... but we orcs would know that more than others.$B$BWe should turn our attention to this Tortusk problem.',0),(13967,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $R.$B$BThis should keep them licking their wounds for a time.',0),(13968,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, so Tortusk behaved as I expected? Went right for your throat? It is good that he\'s dead.$B$BThe Razormane quilboar have been separated from their leadership in the southern Barrens, no doubt allowing an animal like him to come to power. Perhaps without his influence we can start a dialogue with the survivors... Although hotter heads may prevail.',0),(13969,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This poor battered kodo looks to be on the verge of death, but is still breathing. The Razormane haven\'t even plundered its cargo yet. If it can be revived, you may be able to save the entire shipment.',0),(13970,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Kodo is voracious! You might as well be pouring those sacks of grain into a hole!$B$BAlready the animal is beginning to perk up.',0),(13971,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So that was your handiwork, $R? Yes, the missing Kodo arrived just minutes ago. It will take many nights to nurse the poor beast\'s wounds, but thanks to you it\'s alive. And you saved a whole shipment!$B$BPlease, take your pick of the gear that the kodo was carrying.',0),(13973,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see you\'ve left a string of corpses in your wake, $R. I couldn\'t have done better. The livestock may be lost, but the land remains ours - thank you!',0),(13974,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well, look at this! Little Tweedle has really come through this time. This stuff blew up Astranaar, you say?$B$BAs you can see, we don\'t need any help taking over Silverwind Refuge, but Tweedle\'s ideas are as small as his hands.$B$BIf this stuff\'s really as good as you say, there\'s no limit to what we might do....',0),(13975,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s about time we got some supplies through here. It\'s bad enough to be severed from Mulgore, but this city would fall apart if we lost our trade with Orgrimmar.',0),(13977,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Jinx examines the powder carefully for a moment.>$B$BHmmm.$B$BIt\'ll take a little time. But yes, we can put this into a bomb....',0),(13980,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, friend.$B$BYour skills have bought us the time we needed to prepare the bomb. It\'s almost complete!',0),(13983,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This looks right, $C.$B$BI should have your shredder put together in no time.',0),(13988,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am glad Tonga was able to witness the overgrowth firsthand - words can\'t convey the scope of the damage. Did you bring his totem? I will return it to him when I am finished here.',0),(13991,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I was hoping for a squad of grunts... but if you earned Sergra\'s respect, I suppose you\'ll be more than enough. Let me explain what\'s happening here.',0),(13992,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, ho! That was beautiful. I probably shouldn\'t have stayed to watch. Now that they\'re looking for you, I\'ll slip quietly away in the dust of their aimless gallopin\'.$B$BBe sure to look for my buds at the other pools. Boss has agents at every one.',0),(13995,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Aw mon, why you have to go settin\' Gorgal off like that? Still, I can\'t argue with results. We\'ll need to watch these animals closely to see what they do with Kurak outta the way.$B$BMore watchin\' and waitin\'. Gorgal won\'t like that.',0),(13998,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Explosive spore clouds? You don\'t say ... tell me more. Choking? Stinging? Burning of the eyes? Was there itching? Nausea? Mortification? Delightful, DELIGHTFUL! You\'ve certainly earned your commission, $n.$B$BThat skin rash of yours should pass in a day or two.',0),(13999,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Quiet! Give me those notes. Were you followed here?',0),(14001,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, thank heavens that you survived, $n! I thought for sure that you\'d drowned when I saw you go over the side!$B$B$B$BLook at all of these folks you saved!',0),(14003,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sputtervalve scored us a Samophlange? Lemme see that thing!$B$BYeah, we can get this working again, no problem. Hand me that huge mallet...',0),(14004,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wenikee said what? Copperplug? BOSS Copperplug? Oh no, this might be tricky.',0),(14006,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You found it! Wow, it\'s over 600 pages, only 30 of which are intentionally left blank.$B$BLet\'s see. Chapter three: Backsplicing the Reverse Crankshaft Flywheel Pulley? Interesting. Chapter seven: Valve Timing for the High-Pressure Expansion Condenser!? This stuff is great! And I still don\'t even know what this thing does.$B$BHere, have some of my old tools. Let\'s fire this thing up one last time!',0),(14007,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There you go, boss! Come back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know. ',0),(14008,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There you go, boss! Come back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know. ',0),(14009,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There you go, boss!\r\n\r\nCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),(14010,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),(14013,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$C-Matic NX-01 is programmed to serve.$B$BReturn anytime you seek more training. This unit will teach you what it knows.',0),(14023,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Превосходно! Это то, что надо. Конечно, нелегко накрыть такой огромный стол, но праздник того стоит.',19243),(14024,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Тыквенный пирог идет нарасхват – первый раз вижу, чтобы дворфам так нравилось что-то, приготовленное из овощей.',19243),(14028,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Наконец-то, клюквенный соус прибыл! Ты не поверишь, как быстро он кончается.',19243),(14030,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Спасибо за доставку – я уже начал волноваться.$B$BСлушай, пока ты здесь, может, займешься приготовлением засахаренного батата?',19243),(14033,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, candied yam! It\'s my favorite delicacy! Didn\'t Isaac say otherwise?',19243),(14034,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, this is it - this is it right here! So his flagship is named \"The Bellipotent\" eh?$B$BLet\'s see what it\'ll take to send this nuisance to the bottom of the sea.',0),(14035,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are beautiful and just in time to feed hungry feasters. Thank you, $n. You\'ve truly mastered all the courses of a traditional Pilgrim\'s Bounty meal.',0),(14036,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'If you\'d like to learn to cook Pilgrim\'s Bounty foods, I can help. If you\'re not already a cook, all you have to do is train and you\'ll be cooking in no time.',0),(14037,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s a chore keeping all these tables stocked. If you stop and think about it, it\'s strange going to so much trouble when we needn\'t eat anymore.$B$B<William shrugs.>$B$BTradition is tradition.',0),(14038,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent! I wish I could\'ve seen the look on that Rear Admiral\'s face when his flagship went up like a candle. Let me use my telescope here to take a look at the damage.$B$BWhat - Whhhaaatt!? That thing is still floating? Hartley must\'ve moved the munitions ashore in case his ship was mined.$B$BI underestimated you, Hartley... but for the last time!',0),(14040,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The pie always goes first. I think people must be skipping the meal and going directly for the dessert. Have you given it a try yet?',0),(14041,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more cranberry chutney! You wouldn\'t believe how fast the celebrants go through it.',0),(14042,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah! Beautiful work, $n. Those Alliance cretins will never trace this back to me. Meanwhile, it\'s back to business as usual: smuggling, double-dealing, price-gouging... I\'ve got a lot of work to catch up on.$B$BHere, I\'ll let you in on a cut of my future profits. Enjoy!',0),(14043,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So Dokin drafted you to help with the candied sweet potatoes?$B$B<Francis smiles.>$B$BIt\'s the only way he can keep up. Thanks for bringing these.',0),(14044,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks for bringing everything. Some of the tables were starting to look a little bereft of serving dishes.',0),(14045,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah-har! So ol\' Gazzy ain\'t given up on his goods yet, has he? Well, looks like that ol\' floppy-eared goldgrubbler jes\' gave me somethin\' ta bargain with.',0),(14046,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The Baron rubs his sore wrists, his face widening into a malevolent grin.>$B$BOh I won\'t be runnin\' off just yet. I\'ll free me mates and murder my way out of here at a time of me choosin\'. As fer you - a deal\'s a deal. Let\'s talk about that treasure...',0),(14047,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These look perfect. Thank you, $n. You\'ve truly mastered all the courses of a traditional Pilgrim\'s Bounty meal.',0),(14048,1,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Это то, что надо! Спасибо, $n, ты меня $gспас:спасла;.',19243),(14049,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? What is this? I send you out to fetch my treasure and you bring me a big filthy head?',0),(14050,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, $n!$B$BOh, the Baron tried to stop you, did he? Well, I hope you gave him a pounding.$B$BNow, I promised you a cut of the goods you recovered. Let\'s see... what\'s one percent of a half percent? Ah, here you go.',0),(14052,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey hey mon, did Dizzywig send you? Good, good. Did you bring the money? No? ...what about the guns?',0),(14053,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Спасибо, $n. Надо же, ты $gсправился:справилась; быстрее Джаспера – только ему об этом не говори.',19243),(14054,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Отличные пироги! Исааку и прочим гостям они очень понравятся!',19243),(14055,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Превосходно! Спасибо за помощь, $n. Эллен будет счастлива, что мы управились вовремя.',19243),(14056,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Look at that. We\'re loaded! In mutiny, you gotta make the money first. Then when you get the money, you get the power. Let\'s go get some power, $n...',0),(14057,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Tony unhinges one of the weapons and peers down the barrel.>$B$BOooh, very nice. Shiny. Loud. Now we\'re talkin\'.$B$BNot much left to do but close the deal...',0),(14058,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks, $n. Now, I can help the hostess out and still keep my word to Roberta.',0),(14059,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks for your help, and let me know if you ever get to the bottom of the case of the disappearing chutney.',0),(14060,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are great! Thank you for helping, $n.',0),(14061,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These turkeys are exactly what I needed. Thanks for helping me out of a tough situation.',0),(14062,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Perfect timing! I wouldn\'t be able to serve the feast without spice bread stuffing.',0),(14063,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So Tony is running the show there now? Good! We need more pirates like him in these waters. He\'s a real businessman.$B$B<Dizzywig rubs his hands together greedily.>$B$BSpeaking of business, I suppose I owe you a cut. Would you be interested in insuring any of your new loot? You never know what can happen in a town like this...',0),(14064,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, what a feast! $B$BThank you for the $gjoined: joined; to the feast of the feast of the wanderers!',19243),(14065,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What a feast, hmmm?$B$BI\'m so glad you could celebrate the spirit of Pilgrim\'s Bounty with us.',0),(14066,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This Horde caravan was not merely robbed. It was savagely brutalized. Crates of supplies have been ripped apart by sharp claws. The wagon has been demolished. The food has been eaten and the silver is gone, and yet useful supplies have been left behind...',0),(14067,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Gazrog opens the lockbox and begins counting up the silver while you relate your story.>$B$BWhat!? Raptors? Just the raptors? Assaulting our caravans and looting them? Perhaps they are as intelligent as the rumors say. As if we didn\'t have enough problems, now we\'ve got to deal with brainy lizards with a lust for coin.$B$BHere, $n - you\'ve earned a share of the rescued silver. Thank you.',0),(14068,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hooway! You twapped the waptors I was wooking for! Now we will twain them for twolls to wide to swaughter the Awwiance!',0),(14072,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $n. Did you look through these? They\'re barely legible - more like angry graffiti than war plans. Hatred, jealousy, rage, personal conflicts - it\'s a wonder Verog can keep these centaur from killing each other, much less form them into an army.$B$BWe can use this to our advantage.',0),(14073,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, I\'ve heard about your work, $C. Your timing is fortunate - I\'ve got a major offensive in the works.',0),(14103,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful! Another batch of powder!$B$BJust between us jewelcrafters, I\'ve been making hand over fist selling \"pure titanium\" jewelry to the local Dalaran mages. Even with their superior intellect, they aren\'t particularly savvy with their gold. If you get more, I\'ll be here.',0),(14109,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, you are going to look so fine, but not as gorgeous as me! You\'re going to replace the Trade Prince any day now at the rate you\'re going!$B$BI can\'t wait to not have to work anymore! You\'re going to buy me everything that I want, right babe?$B$BLet me have all that stuff and I\'ll help you get into it right before the party.',0),(14113,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very nicely done, sir. The party appears to have been a smashing success!$B$BEr... what\'s that?',0),(14117,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent. As their scouts fail to report in, Talrendis will feel the terror they\'ve tried in vain to inflict on us.',0),(14118,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Meat - and lots of it! Well done. This will keep bellies full as we build our arsenal.',0),(14127,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Ag\'tor squints at the parchment, turning it in the light.>$B$BNo, I can\'t make sense of it either, but I don\'t like what I see. Are these arcane runes?$B$BI\'ll need you to deliver this to an expert.',0),(14128,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? Give that here, this instant! Ag\'tor is correct, these are arcane runes. They\'re scouting out magical sites? Experimenting with the arcane arts? This is a marked departure from thousands of years of night elven history.$B$BHmph! The idea that they will achieve any competence in this field - even those who once counted themselves among the highborne - is absurd.$B$B<Malynea puts aside the scroll dismissively, but her face is furrowed with concern.>',0),(14129,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Labor Captain Grabbit\'s voice crackles over the radio.>$B$BHey $n! Are you reading this?$B$BPiloting that sucker is easy. Push the pedals for your pedal controls and, ah, move the levers for your lever controls. Got it?',0),(14130,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hello there! A new friend! So glad to meet you. My name is Ergll. The g is silent.',0),(14131,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Beautiful beans! They smell absolutely delicious, don\'t they?',0),(14132,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Too mean? Naw, not too mean. They deserved it.$B$BI don\'t gum up their plants. Not ever.',0),(14134,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great! You\'ve loaded the shredder to capacity. You\'re getting pretty handy with that thing...',0),(14135,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great work, $n! That\'s how we took care of business back on Kezan.',0),(14151,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very good, $n.$B$BNow, the trick is to align the facets just right...',0),(14155,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it, $n! The invaders have pulled back. And they told me I was crazy for installing a grenade launcher on a woodchipper...$B$BGreat work with the Shredder. With an impressive showing like that right here on the Warchief\'s doorstep, the Horde can\'t doubt what goblin technology can do for them. I owe you a big thanks!',0),(14161,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good. One less nuisance to worry about.',0),(14162,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re here to help? Excellent! Here, sign this indemnity waiver. And here, this noncompete clause. Let\'s get you started!',0),(14165,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well well, let\'s take a look at what we got here...$B$B<Horzak examines the shattered remains of the poor petrified miner.>$B$BBah! Crumbly! Useless. Wouldn\'t even make a good countertop. My miners may be mediocre workers, but they make lousy bricks.$B$B<Sigh>. Well, I suppose we should re-fleshify these guys so I can get some return on my investment.',0),(14166,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14167,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14168,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14169,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14170,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14171,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14172,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14173,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14174,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14175,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14176,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14177,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),(14190,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Zignibble\'s voice squawks over the speakers.>$B$BIs that you, $n? Still alive? You aren\'t trashing my explosive stockpiles are you?$B$BHmmm... you say you found a clear crystal pendant. That makes sense. A perfect prism would refract the gaze of the basilisk. Maybe we can use this to our advantage. Time to drop some science!',0),(14192,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You pop out the lens assembly and slide the crystal into place. The weapon hums ominously.>',0),(14194,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, good. Now we can get these slackers back to work. You\'ve earned a cut of the profits though - minus the usual company fees. Take your pick!',0),(14197,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done! When it comes to iron, always pick quantity over quality.',0),(14201,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Malynea furrows her brow and begins sifting through the artifacts you brought her.>$B$BSo the spirits of the dead still haunt those old stones, hm? Well $n, as it happens, I\'m counting on their help. Let\'s see what the dead have to say...',0),(14202,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Beautiful work! Now that we know the area better, we can tear this lake a new one.',0),(14209,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Busted ball bearings! Look at this stuff - ugh, SMELL this stuff - my poor, poor dozer!$B$B$n, I consider myself a goop expert and this here goop ain\'t natural. It\'s supernatural. This is ghost goop. We\'re going to need more than a mechanic...',0),(14215,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You reel as the spirit\'s vision fades, relieved to once again feel the earth beneath your feet and the comforting rhythm of your own quickened heart.',0),(14216,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A Sarcen stone? That\'s the stuff of legend - let me see that!$B$B$n, Sarcen stones are used to redirect the ley lines of magical energy. You realize what this means? The mages of Mennar weren\'t staying behind out of misguided loyalty. They sacrificed their lives in order to create this artifact in an attempt to draw energy away from the portal through which the demons were flooding Azeroth. They were buying time for the rest of the world to fight back! History never recorded their deeds. What a discovery!',0),(14226,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Archmage Xylem appears to be doing some kind of dance as he turns to you.>$B$BDo not fret, and better yet, do not forget, to do not let the bug juice set or you will regret... well, you\'ll regret the smell of your boots really! It won\'t smell good today and it won\'t smell good even more tomorrow!',0),(14230,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Peachy. Back to work then.$B$BThanks, snookums.',0),(14249,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ha ha! Perfect! Let me toss this together really fast. The Archmage is sure to be taken in by my style!',0),(14250,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work. This should keep us for another few hours before we have to go back for more.$B$BHe doesn\'t seem to be the brightest of giants. I expect we\'ll be able to keep doing this for a while before he catches on.',0),(14258,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sweet! Beautiful! Brilliant! Who loves you?$B$BWith my mortars re-supplied, I can help you as you assault the Naga east of here. Use these markers to call in an artillery strike anywhere on the cliffs, and I\'ll splatter the whole area with fiery hurt. Oh delicious, merciless, random destruction! I hope you\'re well-armored...',0),(14261,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? So you didn\'t bring any of the drake pieces back? Disappointing.$B$BI knew I should have made you sign a contract before I sent you out...',0),(14262,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Torg scans the horizon.> And still they come! They are like a plague, $n. But with strength like yours, we will crush them. Someday.',0),(14263,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Perfect. It\'s quite interesting how useful the most random things end up being to incantations of this sort.$B$BSo much more to learn!',0),(14267,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The stone in the center of this shrine emits a faint glow and roars with the power of the angry sea.',0),(14270,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The keystone shard slides into place and previously invisible runes suddenly erupt onto the surface of the stone, shimmering in blue and violet hues. Your knees buckle as powerful arcane currents suddenly race into your body...',0),(14271,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'An energy barrier, you say? This explains a great deal! I\'ve seen firsthand how Naga leaders have been able to turn aside the blades of some of my best warriors.$B$BNow we know the source of their power, $n. Let\'s finish this!',0),(14274,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes!  You can feel the power, can\'t you?',0),(14276,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Очень хорошо, $N. Скоро воргены пожалеют о том, что ступили на эти земли.',0),(14279,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are blessed, $n.  The Light shines upon you, even in these dark times.',0),(14295,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now THAT is how we used to handle serpents back in Durotar - we crushed them under our boots! You have done the Horde proud, $n. As soon as my reinforcements arrive we\'ll mop up the rest of those vermin and claim this peninsula once and for all.',0),(14296,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is in this moment that most of my apprentices wonder if there was a logical purpose to storing the energy for my portal in those conduits so that it has to be collected in such a fashion.$B$BOf course there\'s a purpose! I wish to study your behavior... your strategies, your mistakes, your frustrations, your triumphs. Those are the entire point of these trials.$B$BNow, more. More trials! Doesn\'t that sound exciting?! Of course it does.',0),(14297,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks there, pal. Here\'s your commission.$B$BIf you\'ll excuse me, I\'ve gotta get these slackers back to work.',0),(14299,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome! You seem to have survived the trials relatively unscathed. Good for you, love.$B$BYou look to have come with a purpose in mind as well. A question. Your thoughts are very loud, it\'s hard for me to not hear them.$B$BGo ahead then, hon. Ask away.',0),(14300,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Woo! Good for you! That trial really put a fire under your bottom.',0),(14322,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So the world is safe for science again? Excellent! Next time I\'ll try heated needles or something.',0),(14323,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve collected all of the simmering water droplets that Ergll requested. Now it\'s just a matter of summoning the \"jumbo\" elemental.',0),(14324,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Convenient, no? Who needs hot springs anyway. This is perfect.',0),(14340,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well look at you, aren\'t you just a marvel of modern Magery! Quite a fancy hat, I must say.$B$BApprentices. Apprentici? I do think that I might have quite a few already, but I suppose one can never have too many appren..tici.',0),(14345,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Look buddy, I was in your shoes not a week ago. Big powerful Archmage actually takes on apprentices! Who could pass up an opportunity like that?!$B$BSometimes, things really are just too good to be true.',0),(14349,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Grand Crusader sits safely in the Scarlet Bastion while his forces pour into our lands, desecrate our structures and monuments and murder our people.$B$BThe time has come to deal with this pest. You will become the instrument of our reckoning.',0),(14350,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Nathanos laughs.>$B$BExcellent! Finally! An opportunity to destroy the Scarlet Oracle!',0),(14351,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So you\'re the $C who tore through the Alliance forces in the Hillsbrad Foothills? I\'ve heard your name already. Word travels fast.$B$BThe Horde can use someone like you if you keep this up, $n.$B$BWe need to keep our eyes on all threats around us, but with that king leading them, the humans will continue to be a problem. You\'ve confirmed that there\'s strength enough in the Horde to end that threat in time.',0),(14352,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ve seen the insignia on this scroll before during my time in Northrend. You say this was on that crone who leads the pigs in Razorfen Kraul?$B$BI\'ll be damned if I\'m going to let the Scourge get a foothold here. The one who wrote this - this Malcin - is one of the Lich King\'s servants, obviously, and that makes him a target. Your target.$B$BThey\'re not going to take Kalimdor.',0),(14353,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $C!$B$BYou\'ve done the Horde proud by stopping the Scourge from setting down roots on our soil. An act like that deserves a reward, and the Forsaken have enough lying around that I\'m sure they can spare a few things.$B$BWe may not know everything they\'ve done in the Downs, but we\'ll find out. They can\'t slink around in the dark forever.',0),(14355,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m sure Sylvanas will be glad to have that problem taken care of, $n. The task I gave you wasn\'t easy, but here you stand, victorious. That commands respect, and what you\'ve done won\'t be forgotten.',0),(14388,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So scaring him didn\'t work, either? Double-nertz! I\'ll have to break the news to Grapplehammer: Azsharite\'s going to remain the rarest substance on the planet. We\'ll have to use it sparingly.',0),(14389,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Azuregos! At last you\'ve found him!',0),(14390,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Azuregos has agreed to rendezvous with Kalecgos. Success!',0),(14391,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great to see you again! Thank you for finding Azuregos and sending him to me.$B$BI do feel I owe you an apology - I may have undersold how difficult it would be to accomplish the task I gave you. You performed quite admirably, $n.',0),(14392,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey there... again.$B$BLook, I gave you my hat. It was a gift. I thought you\'d make some use of it. More specifically though, I thought you\'d get it the heck away from me.$B$BCan you imagine my surprise when Xylem comes by himself to give it back to me? \"Want to be more like my other apprentices, Sorata? Give your hat another try.\" Not one of my proudest moments.$B$BSo what... you just tossed it aside for him to find? No. I don\'t think so. You\'re going to take this hat and you\'re going to like it. Really.',0),(14407,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you for coming. I apologize for the discretion, but it\'s extremely important that I not be seen by certain individuals.$B$BI\'m in quite a bind and I\'ve taken notice of some of your recent deeds. Hear me out, help me, and I\'ll see to it that you\'re rewarded in kind.',0),(14408,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The raptor snatches the paperwork in her prehensile claws and holds the schematics up to her face, clucking her pointed teeth dismissively.>$B$BThese are like the scrawling of children. Common sense precludes the routing of control hydraulics so near to the secondary stage burners! Still, this is salvageable.$B$BDo you know how to refactor fuel matrixes for pressure variations at a fixed acceleration? No? Very well, perhaps you can do something else for me while I reconfigure the rocket...',0),(14410,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome to Feralas, $C. I thank you for coming to assist us.',0),(14413,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Here so soon! Lovely trip I hope. Not too nauseous or anything?$B$BThere will be much running and much jumping, so a settled stomach is of great practicality.',0),(14422,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful! Exemplary work, $n! As you have no doubt surmised, my objective with regard to this rocket is to utilize it as a sort of astral cradle, an ark if you will, allowing my newly-forged race to slip the surly bonds of this ravaged planet and colonize a world to our own liking. You have been instrumental to our cause. Please accept this currency as I will be minting my own monetary units upon arrival. Farewell, $n!',0),(14423,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? ...What?$B$BMargene! Oh my sweet Margene!!',0),(14424,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What is Clubnik talking about? Haunted construction equipment? Does it look like I have time for ghost stories?$B$BI\'ve got a laboratory in the middle of a meltdown, fires burning, animals mutated, and worst of all - projects falling behind schedule. Help!',0),(14428,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Amberwind was making use of an Arcane Construct? Hah! How delightfully inexperienced. It\'s like watching children play with firearms.$B$BLet\'s take a look at that journal, $n. Hold it up to the scrying stone... keep it still ...',0),(14429,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work getting those runestones. To be honest, I only needed one, but the thought of so many night elves slain for such useless baubles fills me with a dark, giddy joy.$B$BPlease hold one of those runes up to the scrying stone to let me see. Hmmm. As I suspected, an amateur effort at best.',0),(14430,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Haha! Hah - HA! Night elf \"mages\" fleeing their own arcane creation. Your actions have made my month, $n. That\'s why we blood elves don\'t use arcane constructs anymore - they\'ve been outlawed for, oh, 1500 years. It\'s amusing to me to watch our foes repeat the mistakes of the past. \"Mages.\" Indeed.',0),(14431,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see... This definitely looks like a working draft of some sort of treaty. That\'s a worst-case scenario for us, $n: Night elves coordinating attacks with entrenched furbolg allies.$B$BMy initial instinct - a full-out frontal assault - would only drive them into the arms of the Alliance. We will have to take a different approach...',0),(14432,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah good, that\'s plenty. We\'ll boil this stuff up and you can bask in the fumes for a while - you\'ll be speaking like a furbolg in no time. Our plan is beginning to take shape...',0),(14433,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work! Let me see those documents. Hmm. Now we know exactly when and where the final negotiations will happen. Don\'t worry if those robes don\'t fit you - I\'ve got it all worked out.',0),(14435,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Victory! The Blackmaw won\'t know who to trust anymore.$B$BWith that delicate bit of business complete, I can orchestrate a full-on assault against those beasts without worrying about them siding with the Alliance.$B$BYou do good work, $n. Perhaps we should place you in the Horde diplomatic corps? Hah-har!',0),(14442,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Have you come to assist me with my work? My claws are quite dexterous, but I must reluctantly confess that my arms are debilitatingly short.',0),(14443,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Caladis takes the hilt from you and slowly turns it over in his hands.>$B$BThis seems somehow familiar, as though I should know its origins. You say you recovered this in the citadel? Most intriguing.$B$BThere are few who possess the ability to make such a blade. Perhaps they can tell us something about your find.',0),(14444,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We can\'t let that book remain in Sunreaver hands. If we hope to identify the sword and use it to our advantage, we have to find a way to capture the book Krasus lent them.',0),(14457,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Arcanist Tybalin examines the captured orders.>$B$BThe agent you intercepted was supposed to transport the Wyrmrest Tome to Icecrown, after meeting with one Magister Hathorel in Sunreaver\'s Sanctuary. We have to get that book, $n, and this is our chance. It\'s not going to be easy, though.',0),(14462,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re just in time, $C. I\'m about to launch a lightning-strike precision assassination. Let\'s see...$B$BExplosives? Check.$BPneumatic grapplestabber? Check.$BPortable parachute? Check.$BCrippling nerve toxin?$B$B$B$BCheck. Let\'s do this thing.',0),(14464,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m impressed by the cleverness of our new goblin allies, but I\'m even more impressed by you, $n. Look at the gaze of terror frozen onto the Captain\'s face! He never saw your attack coming. Imagine the fear this will cause in Northwatch when they see what happened to one of their precious officers in night elf lands.$B$BWell done, $C. Our assault proceeds...',0),(14468,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Latest recruit, eh?$B$BI\'ll make this short and sweet. We\'re under contract to keep the naga in the ruins from reaching Gallywix or his property. You handle whatever we ask of you, and I\'ll see to it that you get paid when all of your rounds are complete.$B$BWelcome to the Bilgewater Battalion.',0),(14469,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re a light-footed bugger, aren\'t ya? Good work.$B$BHere are a few of the supplies to keep you lively.',0),(14470,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Quick work there, recruit.$B$BShe\'s a beaut, isn\'t she? Assembled her myself. I\'ve got special plans for this baby.',0),(14471,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Can you believe they PAY us to do this?',0),(14472,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'BAM! In the face! Nice shot, kid.',0),(14475,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Reinforcements, at last!',0),(14476,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sweet. Let\'s torch this banana stand!',0),(14477,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, let them burn! Let them burn through the night, so that their flaming tower will light the battlefield beneath us as we rain terror upon their heads.$B$BThank you, $n. Stay close: the invasion is about to begin...',0),(14478,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome back to duty soldier. Good to have you back.',0),(14479,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Bumpy ride?',0),(14480,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your name\'s getting around... nearly Gob Squad status some would say. You\'re a vicious one.',0),(14484,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Glad you\'re on our side, soldier.',0),(14485,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The hope is that that cuts off a major source of their magic. The truth is, we don\'t really have a clue. Who can pass up an opportunity to blow some stuff up though.',0),(14486,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent. Here\'s your cut.$B$BGood doing business with you.',0),(14487,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hahah! It\'s HUGE!$B$BWe\'ll have you take it back to Uncle Bedlam as soon as everything\'s cleaned up here and you\'re ready to go.',0),(20438,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I knew Shandy would find a way to come through for us. Let me get this enchanted and ready for you to use. The sooner you get done with the tabard, the sooner we can get it back to Shandy and the better the chances that its owner will never have missed it.',0),(24430,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh yeah! I love the smell of freshly-cratered dirt!$B$BWord around camp is that the elven front line is collapsing back toward the river. Talk to Chawg and see if there\'s anything you can do to help seal the deal.',0),(24433,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Lok\'tar ogar, $n! As they discover the bodies of their comrades they will learn that no place is safe from the fury of the horde, and their will to fight will crumble.',0),(24434,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Images of a great and distant tree flood your mind. Your stomach lurches as you reorient the stone, briefly filling your senses with visions of a fiery portal, a towering mountain, a frigid wasteland, and a terrible scar across the earth.$B$BAfter a moment, the magical energies of the stone calm, and you feel you are but a step away from Valormok. Andorel\'s invasion can begin...',0),(24435,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good clean fun.',0),(24436,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fine job there, bud. We\'ll have this beach cleaned up in no time.',0),(24437,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah hah! Brilliant. Right fine job there, boy.',0),(24439,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'...Then it is done!$B$B<Chawg surveys the battlefield.>$B$BThere are still pockets of resistance around our camp, but this rearguard action appears to be masking a full-fledged retreat to Ashenvale. Azshara is ours!$B$BThe Warchief will hear of this victory and your part in it. But we will surely need the help of a $C like you elsewhere. Be sure to speak with Kroum here in camp before you leave.',0),(24448,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n! You made it in one piece, good.$B$BWe\'ve got a lot of work for you to handle for us inside the ruins, but we\'re sending you in with the best to take care of it. You\'re working with GAMA Force now, Goblin Army: Mergers and Acquisitions. Molotov says you can handle it - that\'s all I need to hear.',0),(24449,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'And you come with the artifact! The operation was a success then. Mergers and Acquisitions can definitely handle themselves. This thing will fetch quite a pretty penny.$B$BAnd you - I heard you did some impressive work down there. You may well have cut-down expenses by 10% single-handedly. That\'s the kind of smarty businessman I want in my army!$B$BHere are your wages, as promised. And a little something extra too - I hope you like it.',0),(24452,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hahah! Sweet deal. I\'ll get the ball rolling on this. All I need now is to find a buyer and get the go-ahead from Uncle Bedlam.$B$BHere are your wages for your work here. Excellent work, soldier.',0),(24453,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What?! I got left out of the action completely? Are you serious?$B$BAlright, alright... no shooting the messenger. Thanks for the news, bud. Maybe I\'ll see you back at town.',0),(24454,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Caladis accepts the heavy book and begins leafing through it.>$B$BI knew the symbols on the blade were familiar. The weapon was most certainly forged by the dragons and gifted to one of the mortal races, but which blade is this, and how did it come to rest in Icecrown?',0),(24455,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice to meet you soldier. Commander Molotov speaks highly of you.',0),(24458,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh! This is it! It\'s the big one!$B$B<Fizzlefuse calls out to his workers.>$B$BWe\'re in business boys!',0),(24463,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You say Talrendis Point has fallen? That\'s good news!$B$BIt also explains the exodus of elves I\'ve seen along this road.',0),(24467,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You truly amaze me, mortal. It\'s rare to meet someone so dedicated and resourceful.$B$BAzuregos and I are likely to depart Azshara and remain discrete for a while. I do hope that we meet again someday though. Perhaps to put an end to Deathwing himself.$B$BFarewell, $n. Stay safe.',0),(24478,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Brilliant. You certainly don\'t let cold feet stop you. Or cold any part for that matter!$B$BNo? ...too soon?',0),(24479,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I like the way you move, apprentice.$B$BDon\'t you worry about where I got all the souls from. They were obtained in a perfectly humane manner, I assure you.',0),(24494,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are dark days, friend. Look around you... even here in remote Coldridge, the sprits are rebelling. The land is crying out for help. Yet still, even in times such as these, the spirits will always turn an ear to those who ask for their assistance.',0),(24496,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The power of the arcane is everywhere, $n.  Only some of us have the ability to see it, and fewer still possess the ability to master it. You are one of those few. ',0),(24497,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s past time that these night elf scum be purged from Azshara. Glad to have an able body like you to sink the point home.$B$BReady to get to work?',0),(24499,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just in time! Thank you, $n.$B$BThe Pit of Saron lies ahead, and if our scouts are correct, past that will be the Halls of Reflection. It is there that Arthas lets his guard down, and it is there that we hope to find a clue to his weakness... or maybe, just maybe, his redemption.',0),(24510,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n! I\'m so glad you\'ve come.$B$BWe\'ve been afforded a rare chance to delve into Icecrown Citadel, but we must move quickly if we\'re to avoid Arthas\' notice.',0),(24522,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Admit you to the Sunwell? That\'s impossible! The Sunwell is the most sacred and important site of our people. We have only recently reclaimed it with the help of the Shattered Sun Offensive. It is not a place for tourists or travelers.',0),(24526,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There we go!  One spell down, many many more to go.  Come back to me after you\'ve had some experience casting this spell, and I\'ll show you some more tricks. ',0),(24527,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This has been but one of many footfalls on the long path of the $C. Come back to me after you\'ve had some experience in the field, and I will help guide you on your next step.',0),(24528,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There, ya did it.  The Light favors quick learners like you.  Come back to me after you\'ve spent some time using what I\'ve taught ya, and I\'ll show ya something new. ',0),(24531,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now we\'re getting somewhere. You\'ve got quite a manly bellow, sir!$B$BCome back to me in a bit, and I\'ll teach you something else.',0),(24532,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve got the hang of it. Go get some practice out there... maybe take out a few of those troggs or trolls. Or rabbits, I don\'t care.$B$BReturn after you\'ve gotten some practice, and I\'ll show you another trick of the trade.',0),(24533,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n.  You\'ll make a fine $c in due time.\r\n\r\nReturn to me after you\'ve proven yourself a bit more, and I\'ll reward you by teaching you another spell or two.',0),(24545,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A deep sense of dread washes over you as the flame devours the items.',0),(24547,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Highlord Mograine eyes you in silence for a moment.>$B$BYou seem to have endured this leg of your trial admirably, $R.$B$BPray that fate continues to smile upon you in your endeavor...',0),(24548,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These should suffice, $C.$B$BSpeak to me when Shadow\'s Edge has been thoroughly empowered and I will attempt its completion.',0),(24549,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Congratulations, $C.$B$BAgainst insurmountable odds, you have weathered the storm.$B$BI trust that you shall find your reward proportionate to your conviction...',0),(24553,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is unbelievable, $n. You\'ve really done it! All of the quel\'dorei have heard of Thalorien Dawnseeker and Quel\'Delar, but no one ever thought the sword would be restored.',0),(24554,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Myralion takes the hilt from you and scrutinizes the artifact.>$B$BThis came from the citadel? What was it doing there? This blade is certainly not of Scourge manufacture.$B$BWeapons of this quality can only be crafted by a few of Azeroth\'s creatures. We will have to consult them and see if they can help us identify it.',0),(24564,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),(24580,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Word of your success precedes you, $C. Anub\'Rekhan is no more. You did him a great service, $n.',0),(24582,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C. The Scourge military command out of Naxxramas has been thrown into disarray by Razuvious\'s demise.',0),(24583,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Children everywhere will sleep easier knowing that Patchwerk is no more.',0),(24588,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The greatest weakness of Ulduar is its masters\' blind faith in their inventions to protect it.',0),(24590,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Frozen Throne is without its chief guardian thanks to you. Our attacks upon the Lich King\'s forces will be all the more successful now.',0),(24594,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),(24595,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is unbelievable, $n. You\'ve really done it! All of the quel\'dorei have heard of Thalorien Dawnseeker and Quel\'Delar, but no one ever thought the sword would be restored.',0),(24596,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),(24597,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24609,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24610,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24611,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24612,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My \"thanks\" for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24613,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24614,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24615,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),(24640,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya. ',0),(24686,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm... yes, these seeds will do nicely. You have the gratitude of the Cenarion Circle, $n.',0),(24687,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You return victorious. Good, good... perhaps the crater will now be a bit safer to those who travel through it.',0),(24689,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh... did Garl send you? How are his studies coming? I find that he can be a bit slow at times, but he\'s truly a force to be reckoned with when he takes the form of the bear.$B$BNow, we have more pressing matters to attend to.',0),(24690,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'At last, Blazerunner is dispatched. Thanks, $n... he was driving me batty.',0),(24691,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Brilliant! We\'re on the cusp of something big here, $n. Here\'s your share of the inevitably huge profits.$B$BNow, on to other matters...',0),(24692,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve completed a remarkable task, $n. You are truly worthy of commendation. Thank you, and congratulations!',0),(24693,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very well, if Quixxil recommended you, then I suppose you\'re alright. In all our years working together, Quixxil\'s never steered me wrong.',0),(24694,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I have been watching you, $n. Your arrival was not unforeseen.$B$BIn fact, your arrival here has been predetermined for some time now.',0),(24695,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have proven to be both wise and agile, young $n. You have my blessing to take your newfound knowledge and spread it as you continue on your journey.',0),(24697,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n. Now we\'re a bit safer from dinosaur attacks... plus I\'ve got all this fresh meat to serve to my men.',0),(24698,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good ol\' Nolen. How is he doing? Hopefully better than I am...',0),(24699,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, this tar is just the stuff...$B$BHey, wait a minute, my hands... I can\'t seem to get them apart...$B$BMaybe this wasn\'t such a good idea. Oh, but wait! Super sticky tar remover! That\'s where the real money is!',0),(24700,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, there they are. Great work, handsome! Here\'s some gold. You\'ve earned it.',0),(24701,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s a bunch of junk, but it\'s a bunch of FREE junk, and that\'s all that matters to me.$B$BWell, mostly free. Here\'s your share. Thanks!',0),(24702,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You almost sense an air of gratitude as you place the Bloodpetal sprouts on the grave.>',0),(24703,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You please me, $n. From this day forward, you are no longer a simple beggar, but a squire loyal to Maximillian of Northshire. Prepare yourself for our first sally, good squire, for together we shall plunge our fists elbow-deep into what they call adventure!',0),(24704,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'...and that makes 15 of them.$B$BJustice had a name today... and that name was Maximillian of Northshire. For Doloria!',0),(24705,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Our duty is fulfilled. Even so, it troubles me that today\'s damsels were less than gracious... only the fair-haired one by the lake managed to show us any gratitude for our chivalry. Perhaps tomorrow\'s damsels will have thankfulness to match their beauty.$B$BNow we must ride. More adventures await!',0),(24706,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Might I ask you a question? What act have you committed to make the spirits so angry at you? I\'m impressed that you had the patience to sit so still while they pummeled you so violently.$B$BNow we may proceed. The teeth and scales of Un\'Goro\'s greatest dragon await us.',0),(24707,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The day is saved! Huzzah! Today we learned that while armor can be replaced, valor has no price.$B$BBecause of your key involvement in this task, I hereby graduate you from squire to fledgling knight. No longer do the chains of servitude bind you to me; you are free to serve other masters.$B$BGo with honor, young hero! For chivalry, the Light, and the beauty of Doloria!',0),(24708,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What an interesting femur you\'ve brought here, but why\'s it all sharp and curvy?$B$B...$B$BWait a minute, that thing\'s a TALON? A dinosaur with a talon that size would\'ve been... well, really big, that\'s for sure. Is this the only fossil that you found there?',0),(24709,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I knew it! Durrin HAS been digging around here. And he\'s been excavating what could be the archaeological find of the century! Now I just have to find out where he\'s stashing the bones...$B$BThanks $n. You\'ve been a great help.',0),(24714,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A-Me lies motionless before you. No power seems to be running through her components.',0),(24715,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You pour the coconut milk into what appears to be A-Me 01\'s oil reservoir. You hear the sound of gears whirring and actuators firing.',0),(24717,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wow, 2 of each color! You\'re certainly an overachiever, $n. My companions and I could use a $R like you around here. Ever consider a career in profiteering?',0),(24718,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wow, look at this one! Not just the color, but the size of it... you could cover a tauren with this.$B$BHere you go, $n. You\'ve earned this. Stick around, I\'m sure we can find something else for you to do.',0),(24719,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My mentor says that sometimes you have to take away from nature before you can give back. These raptors... I feel that they died for good cause.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),(24720,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now I will continue my experiments! Thank you, $n.',0),(24721,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You were right to bring this pylon to my attention, $n. This is just the sort of thing I\'ve been studying.',0),(24722,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You think this may be related to the attacks on Marshal\'s Refuge, $n?',0),(24723,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A pylon in the west? And a relationship between titans and dinosaurs? This is a lot to take in, $n.',0),(24724,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),(24725,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),(24726,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),(24727,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),(24728,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),(24729,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),(24730,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent, these should do the trick. And now, if you\'ll permit me, in case anyone\'s listening...$B$BTHANKS FOR DIGGING ALL OF THESE BONES OUT OF THE GROUND FOR US AND NOT HURTING THE NATIVE BEASTS IN ANY WAY.$B$BWhether you really did or didn\'t, I don\'t want to know. Let\'s keep it that way, shall we? Here - maybe this will keep your lips shut on the whole thing. Anything to get out of here alive, I say!',0),(24731,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This will do nicely, $n. It seems Lar\'korwi eats well these days. Although, I wonder where he found a threshadon in this area. Odd.$B$BRegardless, I will hold onto this until you are ready for your confrontation with the beast. Do not worry for my safety--I am sure you\'ve angered Lar\'korwi enough that he will not kill me until after he\'s tasted your flesh.',0),(24732,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, fine specimens, $n. The two pieces you\'ve found should be perfect for baiting Lar\'korwi into the open. I cannot wait to see the outcome of your fight with the monster. He is a massive thing with claws as sharp as the finest blades. You will look into his eyes and you will know death.',0),(24733,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Earth Mother be praised! You\'ve done it! Fair play to you, $n. You have proven to be a great hunter in your own right. Your spirit is strong. Your bravery unmatched. And your strength has been fortified. I bow down to your skills.$B$BOnly the greatest of my ancestors could have accomplished something so incredible. Congratulations.',0),(24734,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You find what appears to be Ringo\'s belongings. If he left these here, he can\'t have gone far away. Maybe you should look for him.',0),(24735,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ringo\'s not in the best shape, $n, but I am glad to have him back in one piece!$B$BThank you for finding him.',0),(24736,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, these scales are perfect. I should be able to get this flyer off the ground with these scales for sure!$B$BThanks!',0),(24737,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yeah, this tar is pretty sticky, I guess. I mean, it\'s sticky, but it\'s not \"make fistfuls of money\" sticky. I guess I\'ll have to keep thinking.',0),(24740,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I hope that did the trick. I\'ll take the ash... this may come in handy sometime down the line.',0),(24742,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These results are astounding! My boss will be pleased. Thank you, kind $R!',0),(24743,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Listen well, $C. In accepting this weapon your fate is sealed.$B$BOvercome or succumb.$B$BI have placed your feet upon this path. You are therefore my personal responsibility. Should you failter, I am duty-bound to deliver you from this life.$B$BRemember my words, $R, and do not fail.',0),(24748,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So, at last it is done.$B$BMay the people of Azeroth remember our deeds here forevermore. May the sacrifices of so many burn in their hearts eternally. May they never fail to risk mortal peril in the face of great evil.',0),(24749,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C.$B$BThe completion of our work draws near.',0),(24752,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya. ',0),(24756,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C.$B$BShadowmourne is nearly within reach.',0),(24757,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The axe has drunk its fill, $R, and the forge is nearly ready for the creation of Shadowmourne...',0),(24760,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya. ',0),(24766,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya. ',0),(24772,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya. ',0),(24784,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya.',0),(24794,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? Krakle sent you?',0),(24795,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That a weapon of such power has been redeemed from the clutches of evil is a great omen in these times, $n. With Quel\'Delar and staunch Silver Covenant allies at our side, the Lich King will have good reason to fear.$B$BThe crusade maintains an arsenal of exceptional weapons for our strongest allies. Allow me to offer you your choice from among them in return for entrusting us with the care of Quel\'Delar.',0),(24796,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is nothing short of an amazing accomplishment, $n. The day that Thalorien and Anasterian fell, the same day that Quel\'Delar was lost, was one of the darkest of my life. To see Quel\'Delar restored... it is beyond words.$B$BWithout a doubt, you are meant to be the true bearer of the blade. Quel\'Delar\'s magic is already adapting the blade to your skills and your strengths.',0),(24798,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That a weapon of such power has been redeemed from the clutches of evil is a great omen in these times, $n. With Quel\'Delar and staunch Sunreaver allies at our side, the Lich King will have good reason to fear.$B$BThe crusade maintains an arsenal of exceptional weapons for our strongest allies. Allow me to offer you your choice from among them in return for entrusting us with the care of Quel\'Delar.',0),(24800,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Quel\'Delar rises again, as we sin\'dorei have risen from the ashes of defeat and betrayal. The heart and the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker are both with you, $n.$B$BI see the blade has already started adapting itself to your strengths, $n. Hold your head high and always keep Quel\'Delar at your side.',0),(24801,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Quel\'Delar rises again, as the sin\'dorei have risen from the ashes of defeat and betrayal. Yet, somehow, the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker has chosen to serve an outsider.$B$BBe at ease, $n. I do not mean to diminish your accomplishment, for you have done what none of my brothers could, although I do not know why. You are clearly meant to be its bearer; the blade is already adapting itself to your abilities. Wield Quel\'Delar proudly against our common foes.',0),(24820,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, <brother/sister>.',0),(24821,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, <brother/sister>.',0),(24822,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, <brother/sister>.',0),(24825,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(24826,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(24827,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(24829,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are a true champion of our cause, $n. None can claim to be more dedicated to the struggle than you.$B$BThe enemy speaks of your name only in whispers, for they know you\'re a force to be reckoned with.$B$BAccept this humble gift as a reward for your many triumphs.',0),(24830,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(24831,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are a true champion of our cause, $n. None can claim to be more dedicated to the struggle than you.$B$BYou are a bastion of wisdom and our allies speak of you with the greatest reverence. Many of them owe you their own lives.$B$BAccept this humble gift as a reward for your many triumphs.',0),(24832,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(24833,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are a true champion of our cause, $n. None can claim to be more dedicated to the struggle than you.$B$BIt is rumored that the minions of the Scourge fear you more than they do the Lich King himself. You are vengeance incarnate.$B$BAccept this humble gift as a reward for your many triumphs.',0),(24834,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(24835,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are a true champion of our cause, $n. None can claim to be more dedicated to the struggle than you.$B$BYou are a source of inspiration to our allies and your unshakeable valor gives pause to even the most seasoned of our enemy\'s generals.$B$BAccept this humble gift as a reward for your many triumphs.',0),(24854,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Zen\'Aliri was wise to send you here. I\'ve hit a dead end in my studies.',0),(24855,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The scent of bloodpetal pollen hangs about your head, $C. This is good.$B$BYou\'ve earned your reward.',0),(24865,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh... wow... it\'s some really old food. Hey Hol\'anyee, take a look at this! This $R brought us those old rations that we abandoned!$B$BNo, not from Marshal\'s Refuge... from the old base camp!$B$B$B$BI\'m not sure I want to peek inside. I\'ll just give it to Nolen, I guess... he\'ll know what to do with it.',0),(24866,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well I\'ll be... that\'s Shizzle\'s old portable dinomometer! Where did you find this?$B$BI\'m surprised it\'s still functional, even after all these years. I\'ll have it delivered to Shizzle promptly.',0),(24905,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ve got a great one for you this time, $n. We\'re gonna initiate these ogres into the Horde...working directly under us.',0),(24906,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm, mostly usable. This is good stuff. I\'ve already got buyers lined up, of course.$B$BHere\'s your advance for the rest of the work you\'re gonna do for me and the Bilgewater Cartel...partner.',0),(24907,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Property values have already gone up since you left. People like seafront views that don\'t include briny, gnarled giants stomping around.$B$BHere\'s your cut, $n.',0),(24910,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Isn\'t it nice when you can do a good deed, and see enormous future financial gains from it? It warms my little goblin heart. And my big goblin wallet.$B$BYou did great, kid. Gadgetzan\'s gonna be ours soon. Here\'s a little token of my appreciation.',0),(24911,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey Hol\'anyee, look at the getup on this one!$B$B<Williden turns to face you.>$B$BAhem. Our recruiter sent you? Good. Let\'s start out with a bit of honesty: Un\'Goro isn\'t the perfect nirvana that you may have been promised. You\'ve probably figured that out on the way over here, though.$B$BShall we get to work?',0),(24912,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Stand Clear, $C, and steady yourself.',0),(24913,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am moved, $n. Prophet Velen has been in closely guarded seclusion. He has dared not waste his energy on anything save preparing for the final confrontation he has foretold.$B$BAnd yet, he came here, in person, to comfort a single dying soul.$B$BI must thank you as well, for helping me make my last effort to comfort my friend. My research will continue... and I hope that Magtoor will continue to watch over me.',0),(24914,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<After tracing a complex pattern of runes on each of the box\'s surfaces, the outline of a lid appears and a click echoes through the chamber.>$B$BHere you are, $R.',0),(24921,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hm? What unit are you with, $C?$B$BNo matter, we need all hands. My fleet is in tatters and they\'ve broken into the hold. You armed? That\'s good enough for me.',0),(24926,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'She decided to stay? Fascinating... I\'ll have to look over this data and find out why.$B$BThank you again, $n. I really appreciate it.',0),(24927,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m pleased to report that our brand recognition in this area has skyrocketed now that you\'ve killed most of the people who didn\'t want us here.',0),(24928,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful job. Have you ever thought about becoming a full-time arsonist? I know a few people, it\'s a nice gig.$B$BWell, we\'ll chit-chat about that one later. More to do here!',0),(24934,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You make a hell of a marine, $n.$B$BWe\'ll mop up the others. But it looks like the Horde fleet is disengaging - maybe to land more troops ashore?$B$BAdmiral Aubrey will know what to do. Talk to me when you\'re ready to fly back!',0),(24947,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good thing you\'re here! I\'m gonna need a lot of help if we want to beat these gnomes to the punch.',0),(24949,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Beautiful! And to think these idiots were just sitting on it.$B$BHere\'s a bit up front, we\'ll talk about profit-sharing bonuses later.',0),(24950,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sea giants? You think he was training them towards Gadgetzan on purpose?$B$BWhatever, he\'s splitsville now. And Gadgetzan owes us big time! I can\'t wait to see the look on Marin\'s face.$B$BHere\'s your cut, babe. You\'re moving up in the world.',0),(24955,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wow, nice work! I\'m amazed you even got them to hold a pen without eating it.$B$BYou can uh, just throw the suit over there. Away from me. In the fire.',0),(24957,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ugh! This entire camp is like a sampler course of awful smells.$B$BLet\'s not handle these things any longer than we have to.',0),(24963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good job, you\'ve taught half the ogres here to fear and respect anything vaguely $R-shaped.$B$BIt\'s amazing what a little reward will do to keep people under your thumb, isn\'t it? Here\'s your payment, by the way.$B$B...what\'s with that look?',0),(24966,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re a good student, $n.  You\'ll go far.  If you ever need any further training, return to me and I\'ll happily oblige.',0),(24967,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Trust me, this\'ll be worth the money. And hey - if you need any more training, stop by any time.',0),(24968,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Congratulations... you\'re one step closer to being a master of the dark arts.  Go practice a bit, and return when you\'re stronger.  I\'ll have more to teach you then. ',0),(24969,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have the makings of a great $C, $n. Go, practice what we\'ve discussed, and return when you are stronger. Then I may have more to teach you.',0),(24992,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm... yes, that makes sense.  Since the worgen have come streaming out of Gilneas, I knew it would only be a matter of time before they arrived here in Tirisfal. ',0),(24993,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'To think, they\'ve been right under our noses!  I\'ll put my deathguards on alert... this will NOT happen again. ',0),(25001,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'And that\'s a wrap! Nothing left here for us but sand. Good job, babe.$B$BWell, maybe I shouldn\'t be so hasty. Did you find anything in that ogre den?',0),(25014,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You found that in the ogre den? That\'s...$B$B...nothing to get excited about, I\'m sure! I\'m sure it\'s just...a perfectly benign trinket...that I\'m going to give you precisely detailed instructions on exactly how to handle.$B$B<Megs drops her voice to a whisper.>$B$BKeep your voice down and don\'t wave that thing around.',0),(25017,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $C. We would be hard pressed to face such enemies without your assistance.',0),(25018,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Of all the...you found this in an ogre den? Unthinkable. I\'m amazed they didn\'t try to smash it to pieces.$B$BWith any luck, $C, we\'ll be able to obtain even more fascinating antiquities here...if you\'re willing to help.',0),(25019,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent. The less interference from the Alliance, the better.',0),(25020,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. With that dealt with, we can focus our attentions fully on exploring the gateway.',0),(25030,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Is this Dargol?  He was vicious even in life, with a temper that bit deep and a blade that bit deeper. Undeath has not done him any favors, though it suits his personality. Yes, this was certainly Dargol.  I can sense his malice, even from the remains you\'ve fetched. You have my thanks, $n. ',0),(25051,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is a great relief, $C. Thank you.',0),(25055,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done $n. But for every element that is subdued another one takes it\'s place. The solution we have here is merely a stopgap. Hopefully my brethren in the Earthen Ring are making more headway.',0),(25060,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your reports of their behavior are truly disturbing...but also slightly amusing.$B$BIf only that Dreadshredder wench had escaped on these vessels instead...',0),(25062,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Kelsey takes the journal and gingerly flips through it.>$B$BI\'m trying not to laugh. This is classic. They have no idea they\'re even on Kalimdor!$B$BThese later pages though...something more significant may be occuring here.',0),(25063,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well, gosh, this day just keeps getting better and better! I may actually smile.$B$BWhen you\'re not looking. You\'ve seen enough of that already.',0),(25065,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. The contents of this chest are sure to advance Gnomeregan\'s knowledge base significantly. I believe you\'ve earned a reward.',0),(25067,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'An impressive start. Be prepared for more.',0),(25068,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Marvelous. To think the shapers of our world crafted these...',0),(25069,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This chest lies undisturbed, sealed for thousands of years.',0),(25070,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The chest now grinds open again, the rest of the antechamber fallen silent.',0),(25073,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, young $r. Ya come highly recommended, mon. It\'s nice ta finally be meetin\' ya in person. ',0),(25092,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done $n. But for every element that is subdued another one takes it\'s place. The solution we have here is merely a stopgap. Hopefully my brethren in the Earthen Ring are making more headway.',0),(25094,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not bad. You\'ve got a ways to go, however.',0),(25095,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Rather impressive. Few can bear to see a silithid reaver face to face, let alone defeat it.',0),(25103,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re with Megs, huh? Word is she\'s been pretty hell-bent on making nice with Noggenfogger.$B$BNot like I care. Are you ready to kill some bugs?',0),(25105,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve really saved my skin, $n. Thanks!',0),(25107,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is truly incredible. The hieroglyphs are undoubtedly titan, but the markings below it...$B$BSome of these characters resemble ancient Kaldorei writings. And you say the antechamber was covered in hieroglyphs?$B$BYou\'ve made a find more monumental than any riches, $n. Please, take whatever reward you prefer.',0),(25133,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hm... your report comes at a bad time.  The Burning Blade is no longer seen here in Sen\'jin, but we will be vigilant in our efforts to prevent their return to the area. The orcs are friends of the Darkspear Trolls.  Honorable friends.  We want to help the orcs, but... we need help too. ',0),(25134,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good.  Maybe they\'ll think twice before slacking next time!  Thanks for the help! ',0),(25138,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, where to start... introductions!  I\'m Acrypha - the one who sent you that parchment - I\'ve spent the last several years in an Undercity library, my head in a book.  I learned everything I could about the arcane, and now I\'ve returned home to share it with grunts like yourself. Shall we begin? ',0),(25141,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You won\'t be sorry. The ability to capitalize on the opportunities created by previous attacks is one of our greatest strengths.',0),(25143,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very well. Now that you know how to speak with the elements, we will test your bond with them.',0),(25145,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You appear to be a quick learner. ',0),(25147,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You understand now? Good, let\'s try it out.',0),(25149,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good.  Now we practice. ',0),(25154,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks! I\'m sure to beat out that Marith Lazuria in Orgrimmar with these! I can\'t wait to see the look in her beautiful eye when I give this to her.',0),(25155,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your work is as good as it is rumored to be!',0),(25156,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks. Erm. Just set them over there. I need to figure out how to get my hand off of this jar�',0),(25157,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It did what!? We\'re ruined! Hmm. Well, actually... Maybe the professor can find some other applications for it?',0),(25158,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve really saved my skin, $n. Thanks!',0),(25159,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It did what!? We\'re ruined! Hmm. Well, actually... Maybe the doctor can find some other applications for it?',0),(25160,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks! I\'m sure to beat out that Isabela Jones in Stormwind with these! I can\'t wait to see the look in her beautiful eye when I give this to her.',0),(25161,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your work is as good as it is rumored to be!',0),(25162,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks. Erm. Just set them over there. I need to figure out how to get my hand off of this jar�',0),(25164,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m glad you were here, mon.$B$BToshe be lookin\' like he wants to chase dem down. You should go help\'em.',0),(25165,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is it!  The scorpid juju Bom\'bay been waitin\' for!  Now we gonna fix you right up, $c. You come back to Bom\'bay when you be needin\' a pickup.  Bom\'bay got the spells to fix ya! ',0),(25180,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why would Twilight\'s Hammer take an interest in these tablets? Brann himself wrote that he hardly knows their significance, although he did mention something about becoming one with the earth. I will need to confer with my fellow Explorer\'s League scholars to decipher these as soon as possible.$B$BThank you, $n. Without your aid, these tablets would\'ve fallen into enemy hands.',0),(25181,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why would Twilight\'s Hammer take an interest in these tablets? Their contents are a mystery to our most learned scholars and deciphering them will take some time. If Twilight\'s Hammer knows about these relics and desires them, what more are they plotting?$B$BWe are most fortunate that you protected them from capture, $n.',0),(25191,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What, what!? Can\'t you see we\'re under attack here!$B$B<Gimbleheart snatches the readouts from the survey craft, then stuffs them haphazardly into a duffel bag.>$B$BYes sure of course I\'ll give Nibb\'s findings careful study. Later. From the safety of the Eastern Kingdoms, if I have any say about it!',0),(25197,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve ventured all the way here from Honor\'s Stand? Excellent, we could use your experience here.$B$BThey may have breached the walls, but Northwatch isn\'t going down without a fight.',0),(25209,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have proven yourself to be a trustworthy and dependable ally, $n.',0),(25210,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n. I will study the horns, but the situation has become even more dire since you left.',0),(25211,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll show \'em! Nice work!',0),(25212,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic work!$B$BThe data I received shows the radiation levels are fully within safety range of our suits. That is excellent news!',0),(25215,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It shouldn\'t take long to cleanse the water. Thank you for your help.',0),(25216,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Another fan of the Great Sambino! Come all this way for an autograph perhaps? I\'m far too busy to be signing anything... move along now.',0),(25217,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Another sample. Brilliant! The rocky riches of the sea shall soon be mine!',0),(25218,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ya know, I should have given you a weight belt so that you wouldn\'t just float away, air balloon and all. Lucky for me you came down here with armor and all! Hah!',0),(25219,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you. Seriously. If I would have had to endure another shipwreckee laughing at me, I swear I would have gored someone.$B$BI\'ll let you know if I come up with anything.',0),(25220,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $C. There are still much bigger predators we\'ll have to keep an eye out for, but this will at least give us a bit of peace of mind around the cave.',0),(25221,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Swift work. Very impressive.$B$BThat Fathom-Lord got away... I don\'t see him anywhere. He\'s most certainly the key to finding our captured friends.$B$BI will hunt him down. He cannot stay hidden for long.',0),(25222,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A friendly face! Welcome!$B$BVery kind of you to come check on us. We\'re fine. A naga scouting force did find us, but I\'m pretty sure none escaped. We should be safe for now.',0),(25223,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Я думаю, твои способности… нам подходят. Впечатляюще.',19243),(25224,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Значит, тебе удалось пройти эту часть испытания, Тлетвор тебя не съел, а огненные элементали не поджарили?$B$BДумаю, стоит поздравить тебя с получением низшего ранга.$B$BНу… Поздравляю, рекрут!',19243),(25228,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Torek reads over the scrolls you collected.>$B$BWhoever these people are, they really mean to gain a following. It looks like they\'re having quite a bit of success. They can\'t be allowed to incite the citizens of Ogrimmar to panic and hysteria. We must discourage interest in this group and learn as much about it as we can.',0),(25229,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the best group of potential pilots you could find?$B$BOkay, well, I\'ll see what I can do.  I\'ve been known to turn even the biggest pile of gnarled gears into a smooth-runnin\' fightin\' machine and I expect no less with this lot.$B$BWell, I guess it\'s time to work!',0),(25230,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These events disturb me greatly. My study of the antlers while you were gone has revealed little.$B$BWe must find some way to fix this...',0),(25235,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I saw you drop a few of them from here. Nice work.$B$BHere\'s your reward, on behalf of the Night Watch.',0),(25237,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you once again, $n. I will prepare these for our final task.',0),(25239,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(25240,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),(25241,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The spirits of these guardians will return in time, $n. You\'ve freed them to move on in nature\'s cycle.$B$BNow it falls to us to make sure that cycle is free of corruption and needless suffering.',0),(25242,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are a true champion of our cause, $n. None can claim to be more dedicated to the struggle than you.$B$BIt is rumored that the minions of the Scourge fear you more than they do the Lich King himself. You are might incarnate.$B$BAccept this humble gift as a reward for your many triumphs.',0),(25250,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The corruption has been stemmed! The forest can begin to heal now.$B$BMay you have the blessing of the Earth Mother wherever you go, friend.',0),(25252,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent! Even these fools will soon know that to stand against the Horde means death.',0),(25253,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Anton reads over the scrolls you collected.>$B$BWhoever put these leaflets together knows how to get attention and from the state of things in Old Town, there\'s no lack of interest. We must act before they can build a significant following in the city. I fear they\'ll use their influence to spread panic throughout the city, paralyzing us.$B$BWe\'ve got to get inside the organization and learn as much as possible.',0),(25254,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. Now we must focus our efforts on discovering more about this cult and freeing the people they\'ve conned into joining.',0),(25274,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Прекрасно. Я постараюсь подделать эти документы.',19243),(25275,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n? The $n?!$B$B$B$BThe rumors are already flying about you. I don\'t know if I should be thankful or frightened that you\'re here. At least we don\'t have any volcanoes in Azshara!$B$BHonestly, I can\'t believe you\'re showing your face here... Trade Prince Gallywix has setup shop atop the mountain!',0),(25276,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n-damus? Let\'s hope the parents rewarded us with something other than this creepy little guy.',19243),(25282,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. Now we must focus our efforts on discovering more about this cult and freeing the people they\'ve conned into joining.',0),(25283,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh my.  Their reactions were that different?$B$BNot completely what I was expecting, but I think I have a speech that will do.$B$BJust let me find where I put it...',0),(25285,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',0),(25287,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the final draft, then?  Let me have a look...',0),(25288,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, friend. We are honored that you have decided to embrace the truth and join us. Come, there will be more time to talk later and you have much to learn.',0),(25290,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, friend. We are honored that you have decided to embrace the truth and join us. Come, there will be more time to talk later and you have much to learn.',0),(25291,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You think you\'re ready; for the next step, $n-damus? $B$BLet\'s see what you can do...',19243),(25292,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Alto clenches the bullet in his palm as you tell your story.>$B$BGann? Dead? I ... I should\'ve known. His temper... his recklessness. I knew someday it would get the better of him.$B$BBut it sounds as though you\'ve already gifted him with vengeance. Thank you, $n!$B$BTurn your attention now to Dustwallow. If the Alliance finishes their cursed road through here, all your victories in the Barrens may have been for nothing.',0),(25293,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So you found them? Why did the missing men and women not return with you?$B$B<You tell the blood guard about the responses you received.>$B$BWe cannot compel them to change their minds and return to their families. I will let the families know that the relatives have been found and that they are safe. After this cult is broken up, they will likely return to their normal lives.',0),(25294,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Прекрасно. Этот щенок вырастет столь же сильным и безжалостным, как и его отец.',19243),(25296,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Отлично, $n. Или же мне называть тебя $n-дамус?$B$BДай мне минуту, чтобы все прочесть!',19243),(25299,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ты $gпреуспел:преуспела;, $n-дамус. Ты $gготов:готова; к следующему шагу.',19243),(25308,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s great, $n! This time, you\'ve surpassed yourself.',19243),(25309,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ты на финишной прямой к успеху. Будем надеяться, что не испортишь свой рекорд такой глупостью, как сочувствие или человечность.$B$BДавай же обсудим твое будущее.',19243),(25310,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ладно, $n-дамус. Мы должны показать всем нашим конкурентам, что не сдаемся так легко.',19243),(25311,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Как всегда, блестяще. Ты меня не $gразочаровал:разочаровала;.',19243),(25314,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Прекрасно, $n. Наш план почти выполнен.',19243),(25315,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ты. Ты явно не с ними.$B$BТы – союзник?',19243),(25329,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We\'ve done it! Cho\'gall himself has been utterly humiliated by you. His minions are dead, the Gordok are scattered, and now all will know the might of the Horde! Lok\'tar, $n. You\'ve more than earned your reward.',0),(25330,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Просто умница, $n-дамус. Слуги, которых ты $gвыбрал:выбрала; для меня, вскоре получат инструкции.',19243),(25334,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We\'d all suspected da naga, but I knew nothin\' of the Twilight Cult bein\' beneath the waves. Somehow dey are corruptin\' and pervertin\' the elements, makin\' demselves into dese horrors.$B$BWe goin\' ta have to be fightin\' both of dese threats to stand a chance of bringin\' peace ta Vashj\'ir. We don\'t have da men ta do that yet.$B$BCome, $C, we got much ta do.',0),(25336,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'As my master told me...$B$BUpon a violent death, the muisek of a creature may escape and seek revenge. Shrinking the creatures, as you did, $n, prevents the muisek from escaping. Now we may use it as we please!',0),(25337,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Master always said \"after killing an animal, if we allowed the muisek to escape, it may take the form of an even greater creature.\" This is dangerous stuff. Thanks for helping me with my studies.',0),(25338,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. This is my first time working with treant muisek...',0),(25339,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. You have put an old tauren\'s mind at peace.',0),(25340,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now I know that Edana is truly dead. This heart, I will keep it in memory of what you did here for me, $n. Thank you.',0),(25341,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done. Let me have a look at this.',0),(25342,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What\'ve you got for me here? You said the Gordunni had this?$B$BDisgusting...',0),(25343,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now that you understand the master\'s plan, you must prepare yourself to play your part.',0),(25344,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, I can feel the whelp in there. Let\'s get him out and ask him some questions...',0),(25345,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. Now the spiritual powers of the faerie dragon will be available to us.$B$BI hope you willing to perform another task for me.',0),(25346,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just imagine the possibilities of what we now possess, $n. Along with the materials that you have collected, I will be able to forever trap the muisek of these creatures into whatever I wish.',0),(25347,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You hand Blood Guard Torek the devices that the overseer gave you, explaining the cult\'s plans. Torek\'s eyes go wide.>$B$BCho\'Gall is in charge of the cult? There can be no question then, this is the work of the Twilight\'s Hammer! You won\'t be the only one they\'ve sent into the city to deploy these devices.',0),(25348,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n. Twilight\'s Hammer will think twice before trying to turn our own people against us again. I\'m sure I\'m not the only one troubled by just how many citizens were taken in by their message. Times aren\'t exactly easy, but if you have no honor or loyalty, you have nothing.',0),(25349,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n, but the tale of your hunt troubles me. There should not be so many.$B$BThe sickness is still spreading...',0),(25350,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The apprentice\'s body is cold. He has been dead for a while.>',19116),(25351,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The warchief listens as you tell of your investigation into the Twilight\'s Hammer plot to destroy Orgrimmar.>$B$BYou are a dutiful member of the Horde, $n. You have done well in bringing this news to me. I will personally see to it that our enemies get what they deserve!',0),(25356,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jawn sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',0),(25357,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let\'s hope your efforts prove to be enough of a diversion...',0),(25359,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I remember you. You were there when they attacked us back in the cave.$B$BGood to have you with me, $C. Ready for a little vengeance?',0),(25360,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Does everything down here only come in jumbo size? Oooh! That\'s a thought. Maybe there are some hunky sea goblins around here somewhere.$B$BThanks, by the way.',0),(25361,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful, $C! These will do nicely. There are enough here to make a cloak for Korrin, and possibly even more! Thank you.$B$BI hope the trip wasn\'t too dangerous? The area of Feralas is not known for being forgiving, but you\'ve obviously done well enough.$B$BThank you again, $C.',0),(25362,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Traitors to the Horde and traitors to their own people...$B$BI guess they\'re not all bad. They\'ll make fine drinking flasks.',0),(25363,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is proof of a good start, $n. Your skills as a soldier are to be commended.$B$BYou are not the only one I ask that task of. Many before you have fought them, and in times past, our efforts have kept them at bay. Recently though, their attempts to push northward into our area of influence have increased dramatically. Their attacks have also become more savage... almost as if they were desperate.$B$BI have a plan though, $n, that might settle things once and for all against them...',0),(25365,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Examining the map reveals it to be the battle plans that Hadoken Swiftstrider wants. Numerous arrows that perhaps represent troop movements are drawn on the map, though most seem to be headed toward the south rather than to the north where Camp Mojache lies.$B$BAnother section of the map has a picture of what you think is a large insect of some kind, with various tick marks under it. From the looks of the gnolls, it perhaps represents their losses against the unknown bugs...',0),(25368,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m free...finally! Oh, it feels so good to be free...$B$BOh, you saw, didn\'t you?',0),(25372,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Это ключ к нашему спасению, $n! Мы сможем вдохнуть жизнь в эту землю несмотря на все усилия культа Сумеречного Молота! И все благодаря тем семенам, что ты $gсобрал:собрала; для меня, животным, спасенным тобой в горах, и Лесному сердцу. Представь себе, как сектанты поразятся, увидев, что все их труды пошли насмарку и жизнь победила хаос...$B$BЯ немедленно приступлю к церемонии!',19342),(25373,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n, but there is more work to be done to keep the camp safe. Listen further.',0),(25377,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve discovered lost treasure!$B$BYour mind reels at the thought of what else might be hidden in the depths of the sea.',0),(25380,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. It might be awkward at first, but you will get used to advocating our beliefs in public. It is one way of remembering our obligation to bring the truth to others. We must save as many as we can.',0),(25386,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve been tussling with drakes, eh?$B$BI like it. We need someone who can pull their own weight around here. Are you ready to fight for the Horde?',0),(25387,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am thankful you\'ve come, $C. Our camp is beset by many perils, and yet we must tend to those fleeing the devastation of the cataclysm.$B$BIf there is to be any refuge here, you must help us.',0),(25391,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'As promised, you have your choice, $n. The muisek of the creatures has been forever sealed into the power of these weapons.$B$BYou may now wield their energy as your own. Use it well.',0),(25393,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Curses! We had to fall back. But Thermaplugg\'s lost, and he knows it... he\'s only bought himself time. We hold the surface, and when the radiation clears we\'ll assault and recapture Gnomeregan with a force twice this size.',0),(25395,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank the Makers! It\'s downright pristine. Those orcs couldn\'t figure out the tap-lock, it seems...and couldn\'t hack through the mastercraft work of Ironforge\'s keg-crafters with their crude weapons!',0),(25414,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So you found them? Why did the missing men and women not return with you?$B$B<You tell the captain that they seemed determined to stay for various reasons.>$B$BThen we cannot force them to come home. I can only hope that in time, the cultists will realize the harm their actions have caused and decide to return to their normal lives.$B$BThank you for your efforts, $n. I will tell the families what you found.',0),(25415,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. It might be awkward at first, but you will grow accustomed to advocating our beliefs in public. It is one way of remembering our obligation to bring the truth to others. We must offer hope to everyone, for we all face the end of this world together.',0),(25416,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now that you understand the master\'s plan, you must prepare to play your part in making it a reality.',0),(25417,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You hand Captain Anton the devices that the overseer gave you, explaining the cult\'s plans.>$B$BCho\'Gall is in charge of the cult? Then, it has to be Twilight\'s Hammer! We suspected that they would try to strike again, but no one knew what form the attack would take.$B$BYou\'ve done an excellent job uncovering this plot. Unfortunately, you won\'t be the only one they\'ve sent into the city to deploy these devices.',0),(25418,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n. Twilight\'s Hammer will think twice before trying to turn our own people against us again.$B$BWhat worries me is how many citizens joined their movement without thinking about the cult\'s empty promises. Are times so dire that people will abandon the Light for promises of power and immortality?',0),(25420,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $C. We\'re that much closer to the secrets of Uldum.',0),(25421,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is amazing. These hieroglyphs are undoubtedly titan, but the markings below it...$B$BIf I had to hope, this is the same passage written over and over again in an entire assortment of ancient languages. We might be able to use this to decipher the hieroglyphs! If the antechamber was covered in them as you say, who knows what else we\'ll learn.$B$BI\'d like to grant you a fine reward, $n. We\'ve made the find of the century!',0),(25422,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you! Thank you...$B$BI feel much better. With just a bit more...',0),(25423,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You can feel their anguish, can\'t you?$B$BMy poor friends. At least we can use you to fix things...',0),(25425,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The king\'s face takes on a look of concern, and then anger as you describe the Twilight\'s Hammer plot to destroy Stormwind.>$B$BHow dare they strike Stormwind? How dare they try to manipulate the people of this city against us and the Alliance! If not for your valor this day, $n, our city would not have discovered this Twilight\'s Hammer scheme. You are a true hero of Stormwind and the Alliance.',0),(25439,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to have a real warrior at my side. Too often, my shaman brethren can\'t seem to stomach the work.',0),(25441,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Too often, we are mistaken for druidic types. Perhaps that\'s true for some shaman, but do not let yourself be plagued by the ignorant belief that we are always peaceful.$B$BNothing about what I do is harmonious. I command the elements to my will. There is nothing offered in return. I would have it no other way.',0),(25443,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, yes! Show me the runes you discovered.$B$B\"Vol\'talo Thol\'embaar.\" That\'s the name of your real enemy.$B$BPresumably you\'re dealing with one of Ragnaros\'s generals, sent here to scorch the mountainside and pave the way for his conquest.$B$BI will show you how to crush him.',0),(25451,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Incredible! You may have found the granddaddy of all yeti hides with this!$B$BYou better believe I\'ll pay you for it. I normally don\'t pay that much for a single hide, but I\'m pretty sure I can make something special from it. Thanks for thinking of me on this, $n!',0),(25452,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, excellent! These hides, when given a special treatment, are as resilient as iron I tell you! It will take many tries in order to get the right mix down for the tanning, but I am confident they will bring my mark of quality to the next level.$B$BAs for you, $n... your assistance has proven invaluable to me. Please take your choice from these items I have crafted.',0),(25453,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent, excellent! These are going to work out incredibly well - I can already tell that they\'re going to be much harder when properly cured.$B$BThanks again for your aid, $n. Here - please take one of my latest creations.',0),(25454,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is an incredible find! I believe this is the finest yeti hide specimen I have ever seen!$B$BIndeed, this is certainly worthy of an appropriate bounty. I normally don\'t pay that much for a single hide, but I\'m confident I can make something special from it. Thanks for thinking of me on this, $n!',0),(25456,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sam\'s in one piece then? And his poor assistant Felice? Good to hear.$B$BI hope that one day he\'ll learn to respect the elements as more than just a tool.',0),(25467,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The satisfying sound of a chest unlocking is followed by the sight of once-hidden treasure.',0),(25471,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ello, mon! You look a bit more capable then most of dem coming through here.$B$BCome rest a bit. Make yaself at home.',0),(25476,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, YOU\'RE the great savior of OOX-22/FE! I cannot even begin to express my thanks for your assistance! My homing robot series needs more development, but your recovery has saved me countless hours of extra rebuilding time, as well as many gold pieces in manufacture costs!$B$BPlease, take your choice of any of these items I have. Thank you again for your generous assistance $n, my robots and I are in your debt!',0),(25478,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nyse sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',0),(25479,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thyssiana sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',19116),(25487,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You want a canoe to go out to the salt flats? But, surely the race track has been destroyed?!$B$BNonetheless, for your bravery, you will have the last one!',0),(25488,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'YES?! Do you see me interrupting your fascinating argument?$B$BNo... no, please, go ahead. I\'m sure that your interruption is about something very important. More important than dealing with the survival of everyone here, in fact.$B$B<Fizzle taps his foot impatiently.>',19116),(25489,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Heya, kid, I\'ll be right with ya. Just gotta shut this gnome twerp up first.',0),(25494,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Отлично. Теперь этот парень готов к бою.',19243),(25496,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s how it\'s done!',19243),(25499,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'О. Ты все еще $gжив:жива;.$B$BНеплохо.',19243),(25503,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This item was highly prized by the local gilblin population - even coveted by King Gurboggle, himself!',0),(25504,6,5,0,0,0,1000,0,0,'<Jinky eyes the list of parts and spits!>$B$BI don\'t have even half of that stuff!',19116),(25505,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Heya, pal, mind if I take a look at that list?$B$B<Razzeric nearly spits!>$B$BWhat\'s Pozzik thinking? He knows that I don\'t have even half of that stuff!',0),(25509,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Очень хорошо. Ты хотя бы отличаешь острый конец кирки от тупого.',19243),(25513,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic. I might challenge you to a duel myself someday.',0),(25515,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This\'ll do for a start.',19116),(25516,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is a great start!',0),(25517,71,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s the spirit! You\'re a real credit to the Alliance!$B$BYou know, you can go back in there and do that anytime you feel like it. I highly encourage you to do so!',19116),(25518,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes! You\'re a real credit to the Horde!$B$BYou know, you can go back in there and do that anytime you feel like it. I highly encourage you to do so!',0),(25523,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Отлично! Как ощущения?$B$BОсвоить полет в этом пылающем пространстве нелегко, но другого пути нет.$B$BНадеюсь, ты $gготов:готова; сражаться, $n…',19342),(25524,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank goodness! Now, just a little shove....',19116),(25525,66,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impressive flight, $n! Their dying screams echoed through this forgotten cave light. But our business here isn\'t over...',19342),(25526,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank goodness! Now, just a little shove....',0),(25531,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n.',19243),(25532,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'One problem down. Now to deal with the greater threat!',19116),(25534,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, kid. Any close calls? Did you get grazed?$B$BNo? Good, because we\'ve got more fish to fry here.',0),(25535,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'More help! Superb! We can certainly use it, I\'ll tell you that much.',0),(25536,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you for stepping up to take care of this, $C. I know there are a lot of concerns swarming us right now, but maintaining the safety of the survivors is paramount.',0),(25537,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Superb! Chemicals abound!$B$BMy instantaneous chemical synthesizer is already pre-tested and prepared. Your deployment compound shall be ready in the blink of an eye!',0),(25538,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done my odorific associate. You are both swift and assiduous, if I do say so myself. May your future travels be rampant with inspiration and opulence.',0),(25539,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, indeed. This is an entirely unshameful amount of clams to have gathered. The survivors back at the cave will surely be grateful.',0),(25540,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is wonderful. I will begin cooking them immediately. It is good to know that of our many fears, starvation shall no longer need to be one of them.$B$BI imagine the Admiral will have much work for you. Let me trouble you no further for a while.',0),(25541,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice! Remember, gold is gold, no matter who\'s mouth, nose, or otherwise it\'s been in.$B$BIt\'s all perfectly sanitary after being melted down anyway. Or at least wiped off.',0),(25542,4,17,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it! You did it!$B$B<Jinky grabs you and gives you a big smooch on the cheek! She then regains her dignity and smooths her clothes.>$B$BThanks for saving my Speedbarge, Captain $n.',19116),(25543,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You saved my Speedbarge!$B$B<Razzeric embraces you in a manly hug!>$B$BI can\'t begin to tell you how relieved I am, Captain $n!',0),(25544,1,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Клянусь крыльями Авианы – ты буквально $gрожден:рождена; для полетов, $n!$B$BУ нас не так много времени, нужно вернуться и нанести решающий удар!',19342),(25545,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C!$B$BThanks to you, my men will be ready to confront the enemy when they attack.',0),(25546,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This should help relieve our exhaustion.$B$BAgain, we thank you.',0),(25547,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'No time to address the troops now.$B$BJust as well. They know what must be done.',0),(25548,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ты славно $gпотрудился:потрудилась;, $n. У меня есть для тебя другое задание.',19243),(25549,1,6,66,0,0,0,0,0,'Ты не устаешь изумлять меня своей доблестью, $n. Если так будет продолжаться, может, Хиджалу удастся пережить это испытание.',19243),(25550,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Brilliant job, $n! We\'re about to win the Hijal. $B$BIt\'s an honor to fight beside you.',19243),(25551,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Хиджал спасен, $n. И все это – благодаря тебе.',19243),(25552,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ты хорошо $gпоработал:поработала;, $n. С помощью этого черепа мы выманим матриарха сумеречных драконов.',19243),(25553,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It went... better than expected.',19243),(25554,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Этим нечестивым книгам нельзя позволить существовать. Однако имеющаяся в них информация жизненно необходима нам.',19243),(25555,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is done. You have only one step left to complete the mission.',19243),(25556,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Mazoga\'s ghost gives you a blood-smeared grin.>$B$BHow you doin\', mon?',0),(25558,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Earthen Ring has received my distress message and sent help - just in time it would seem.$B$BHopefully more can be sent soon. We are but few against a great many.',0),(25559,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll teach the Horde twofold! Don\'t mess with dwarven history, and don\'t send a bunch of frail couch-dwellers to do your fighting!',0),(25560,1,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s what I call a decisive blow!',19342),(25561,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it! You did it!$B$B<Jinky grabs you and gives you a big smooch on the cheek! She then regains her dignity and smooths her clothes.>$B$BThanks for saving my Speedbarge, Captain $n.',0),(25562,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You saved my Speedbarge!$B$B<Razzeric embraces you in a manly hug!>$B$BI can\'t begin to tell you how relieved I am, Captain $n!',0),(25563,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25564,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Everything here seems to be in working order.',0),(25565,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Would you take a look at these...not troll, not qiraji, just pure mystery waiting to be unlocked.$B$BThese aren\'t going anywhere now that they\'re safely in our hands. It\'s time to make our way into the ruins!',0),(25566,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This chest lies undisturbed, sealed for thousands of years.',0),(25567,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25568,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25569,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25570,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25571,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, $n, this shard does explain the occurrence of the rifts. The elemental planes have been in chaos in Outland ever since Draenor was destroyed. These shards cause a weakness in the already damaged elemental planes and allow the elementals to cross over.$B$BWe\'re still collecting information on who or what is behind all of this. However, the more shards you bring me, the better prepared we will be to fight the elemental invasion here in Azeroth.',0),(25572,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25579,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $C.$B$BI will get some of our own patrols out to make sure that no more naga get within sight of this cave. We should have the area secured within the hour.',0),(25580,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n, and just in time too. The Admiral just started sending more men out. Strong sword arms to be sure, but I doubt they possess quite the same awareness and finesse that you do.$B$BWe were lucky to have you here when things went south. I suspect you will have a large role to play in things to come as well.',0),(25581,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you so much for taking this seriously.$B$BThis is some of the first definitive proof of other members of the Vashj family. Very interesting. And I\'d never even heard of either of the other two figures you mentioned until now.$B$BSo much of our history was lost during the sundering - it\'s exciting to have a chance at reclaiming some of it.',0),(25582,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is good intel. You have a sharp eye, $C.$B$BIt sounds like the building tucked under the terrace at the far end of the ruins will make a suitable forward post. I will send some men immediately to start defensive preparations and we will reposition there as soon as possible.',0),(25583,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Interesting indeed.$B$BThe remains you describe sound much like the sea vrykul we encountered in Northrend. I highly doubt we will be striking any alliances with their sort, no matter the cause. Still, this information may prove useful in the future.$B$BI will think on it further if time permits. Thank you for bringing it to my attention.',0),(25585,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re still shooting, but not nearly as much! Yeeeeeeeeeaaaaaaaaaaah!',19116),(25586,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re still shooting, but not nearly as much! Yeeeeeeeeeaaaaaaaaaaah!',0),(25588,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll teach those scurvy dogs! You have my thanks, $n.',19116),(25589,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll teach those scurvy dogs! You have my thanks, $n.',0),(25590,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey! Get me out of here!',19116),(25591,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic. I might challenge you to a duel myself someday.',0),(25596,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey! Get me out of here!',0),(25597,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Эй, ты. Я рад, что они прислали для этой операции именно тебя.$B$BНам придется сделать все тихо. Мы не можем рисковать жизнью командира Песни Теней.',19243),(25601,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There you are, $n-damus. I need to talk to you about something. I heard about the accident that happened with our poor friend Okrog. Finally, she\'s nodding and winking at you with a sly wink. A capable disciple than I thought.',19243),(25604,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),(25606,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),(25608,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Brilliant job, $n. We can still win.',19243),(25609,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh yeah! Look at all that booty.$B$BWait a minute... bring it closer!',19116),(25610,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh yeah! Look at all that booty.$B$BWait a minute... bring it closer!',0),(25623,1,5,274,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, Goldrinn said you would come. Your eyes do not deceive you: you proved: it turned out; in the Firelands, in the elemental chamber of molten stone and fire. Our business here is simply overwhelming. $B$B Forget about disagreements with the Horde, it\'s hot enough here. $B$B And take this: here, in the Firelands, Goldrinn\'s fang will allow you to direct ancient forces.',19342),(25624,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, you are the champion Lo\'Gosh promised! Your eyes don\'t deceive you: you have entered the Firelands, an elemental plane of molten stone and fire. We\'ve got our work cut out for us here.$B$BPut aside your differences with the Alliance, there\'s plenty of danger to go around.$B$BAnd take this: the Fang of Lo\'Gosh will allow you to channel the ancient\'s power here within the Firelands. Use it well!',0),(25626,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Minions of the Old God? Two very potent foes have joined forces then. Their hope to defeat the Tidehunter may not be so foolish after all.$B$B$n, we can\'t let that happen. If Azshara defeats the Tidehunter and takes his power for herself, I\'m not sure any number of us could ever hope to oppose her on the seas.$B$BThe first step is clear at least - we need to hunt down the fiend that destroyed our ships. The navy was confident enough to bring in a new fleet, perhaps they have a plan.',0),(25627,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yeah, yeah, yeah... I\'m sure that your little adventure into the cave was very interesting.$B$BHow about we talk about it over drinks back on the Speedbarge once you get me out of this cage?',19116),(25628,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yeah, yeah, yeah... I\'m sure that your little adventure into the cave was very interesting.$B$BHow about we talk about it over drinks back on the Speedbarge once you get me out of this cage?',0),(25641,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done indeed... I\'d expect nothing less from my own daughter. She\'ll make a fine witch doctor someday.',0),(25643,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<As you reach towards the pedestal, you find it empty. A chill fills the room, and you hear a faint voice...>',0),(25644,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Хорошо, что ты $gпринес:принесла; это мне, $n. Оно может представлять для нас большую угрозу, если мы не будем действовать быстро и жестоко.',19243),(25645,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am a fool...I was misled. This is nothing more than a rusted trinket, and my visions have no doubt been fulfilled.$B$BForgive me, $n. But should you meet this demoness again, I pray you will triumph over her as you did Verinias.',0),(25648,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, you\'re here.  Welcome to Azshara, the stage for the next act of the Horde\'s glorious future.  Now get to work. ',0),(25653,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Тебе удалось помочь Тортолле, и это значит, что мы получили могущественного союзника… a заодно нашли недостающий фрагмент этой головоломки.$B$BМужайся, $n. Начинается самая трудная часть наших испытаний.$B$BПора перенести сражение на их территорию.',19243),(25660,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What ya be wantin\'? Oh no you don\'t. I can see ya got Tony\'s spirit with ya, and I want nothin\' to do with it!',19116),(25661,11,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'<Ajamon makes a face at the state of the organs.>$B$BThey\'s gonna have ta do. It not be like he had many friends. Ain\'t that right, Two-Tusk?',19116),(25671,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good. Their blood is on Hellscream\'s hands. Send enough of them back to Orgrimmar in a body bag and the populace of the Horde might react.$B$B<Lord Fallowmere laughs.>$B$BWho am I kidding? They\'re monsters!',0),(25672,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, that\'s disgustin\'!$B$BWe almost there, mon. Just need ta do one more ting!',19116),(25674,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $R. You\'ve proven that you can take down an ogre... no small feat. Now let\'s see if you can take down an Alliance iron mine...',0),(25675,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well today, $n. Not only have you purchased more time before the next ogre attack, but I think you scared some of the captives into working harder.',0),(25676,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Finally... another operative shows up. I hope you\'re loosened up... it\'s time to tango, partner.',0),(25677,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There\'s nothing quite like a big fat kick in the wallet, is there, you Alliance lunkheads?!',0),(25678,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, friend. I like the way you do business.',0),(25679,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, you here already. Stick around for a bit, little $R. We gonna mess with the Alliance.$B$BI love my job, mon.',0),(25680,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So it was a demon? Those miners never seen a demon before? We\'re in the Blasted Lands, mon! Demons are everywhere!$B$B<Tak\'arili sighs.>$B$BAh well... let\'s get on to da good stuff, shall we?',0),(25681,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, mon! Without Hondo, these guys are helpless. Dis mine\'ll be ours soon enough!',0),(25682,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Okrilla glances over the report.>$B$BImpressive, $n. I wouldn\'t have hidden in that box, but otherwise, you have performed bravely and admirably. The battle we won today may not win us any immediate spoils, but the damage you\'ve done to the Alliance will last for a long time.',0),(25683,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Okrilla sent you? Okrilla the killa\'?$B$B<Lynnore listens to your tale.>$B$BLoramus was his name? I\'m sorry to say that we have not seen your demon hunter... but we have ways of finding him.',0),(25684,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent. Now that that\'s out of the way...',0),(25685,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore eyes the blood hungrily.>$B$BMore than enough, and still warm! Now, let\'s get this ritual started, shall we?',0),(25686,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The blood ritual was a success; I can clearly see where Loramus is right now. That is, I can see where the pieces of his body lie...',0),(25687,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see... yes, we can work with this.$B$B<Lynnore looks at the night elf\'s head.>$B$BLoramus Thalipedes, demon hunter. I look forward to meeting you.',0),(25688,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You... you fool! What have you done?',0),(25689,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? LORAMUS?!$B$BOh blast, keep it down, would ya? If my boss gets word that I worked for Loramus, do you know how quickly I\'d be on my rear end?!$B$B<Wazzik takes the rune from you, presses it to his chest, closes his eyes, and nods.>$B$BWell, you weren\'t lying. Let\'s get to work.',0),(25690,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are perfect, $n. Lynnore and I will eat well for the next several days.',0),(25691,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I hope this is what he needs. We probably don\'t have time for you to return and mine any more.',0),(25692,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There\'s no doubt about it, you found demon blood.$B$BLoramus\' requests aside, I\'m sure Dar\'toon is thankful for your efforts. They\'ve been struggling to deal with these demon distractions for some time now.',0),(25693,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is sufficient. If you see Wazzik again, you may tell him that he performed satisfactorily. I will get the bloodmages to work on fashioning the stone knife of sealing. There is no need for questions now. All will be revealed in time.$B$BWhile they work, I have another task for you to complete. Actually, make that three tasks.',0),(25694,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your work is appreciated, soldier.$B$B<The warlord leans in close, and whispers:>$B$B$R... if you\'re still interested, I have one more small task for you...',0),(25695,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re certain nobody saw you? Good.$B$B<Dar\'toon listens to your recount of the information you saw.>$B$BHmph... fairly harmless stuff. Either the Alliance are foolish enough to NOT be planning something against us... or they\'re hiding their information better than I expected. Either way, well done, soldier.',0),(25696,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, traveler. Thank you for responding to my summons.',0),(25697,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore examines the amulet.>$B$BHe was an archmage, I can feel it. I will hold the amulet for you while you collect the rest.',0),(25698,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore hefts the amulet.>$B$BA warlock... and a powerful one at that. I will hold onto this until the time is right.',0),(25699,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore clutches the third amulet.>$B$BHe was a powerful warrior, this one. I will keep the amulet until Loramus is ready to proceed.',0),(25700,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It would seem that we are prepared to face our demon, $n. We have the amulet\'s blessing, we have the stone knife, and I alone know the demon\'s true name: Rakh\'likh. Together, this may be enough to defeat the Defiler.',0),(25701,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see. So this was Loramus\' plan all along.$B$BI suspected correctly, but I suppose I refused to believe it. And now, his final instruction for me makes much more sense:$B$BHe asked me to let you choose from one of these.',0),(25702,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The murloc spirit looks upon you sadly.>$B$BSalt-Flop did not shame himself by running away. Look behind me, and see for yourself.$B$BThe Rockpool had no hope against the naga\'s attack.',0),(25703,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have done well, brave $C. I am pleased... but I am not yet satisfied.',0),(25704,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now we gonna bring Tony Two-Tusk back ta life. You both ready, mon?',19116),(25705,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You make an old murloc proud, $R.$B$BThank you, and may the waves ever lap at your feet.',0),(25706,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The last Rockpool may be taken hostage today and killed tomorrow, landwalker... but they will pass into the underworld knowing that a brave $R avenged their death. Thank you.',0),(25708,92,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Enohar takes a sip off of a freshly-refilled mug.>$b$bAye, you\'ve done well, $g lad: lassie;.  You do the Alliance proud.',19116),(25709,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s a tragedy, what happened on the Shattershore.  They weren\'t even soldiers... just people looking for a new home.$b$bI think we\'ve done all we can, $n.',19116),(25710,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm... not bad.  You\'re quicker than many of my men.  Stick around, $n... I may have use of you yet.',19116),(25711,1,14,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re an excellent asset to the Alliance and the Kirin Tor, $n.  Well done.$b$bWith time, our forces will retake the mine and press these Horde dogs out of the Blasted Lands.',19116),(25712,396,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n.  Thanks to your efforts, I am confident that with time, we will take back the Nethergarde Mine.',19116),(25713,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, the sound of things going boom makes my heart pitter-pat.  You\'ve made this gnome\'s day, $n.',19116),(25714,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My associates were correct to send you to me.  I have a problem which may threaten the sanctity of Nethergarde, and I need someone more capable than most.',19116),(25715,274,274,1,0,0,777,777,0,'You saw worgen?  That\'s bad.$b$bWorgen ghosts?  That\'s even worse.$b$bThose weren\'t Horde ships... they were Gilnean.  And they must have been headed down to Surwich, at the bottom of the Tainted Forest.  That makes a lot more sense.$b$bWe\'ve got to try to help them, $n!  The worgen are our allies!',19116),(25716,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ably done, $n.  Now we see if my suspicions are correct.$b$b<The watcher selects a spell focus and focuses intently on its shadows.  After a moment, he turns back to you with a look of horror on his face.>',19116),(25717,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n.$B$BI should be a bit more up-front with you. The demons were a nuisance, but they are not the real problem. That worgen druid is our problem.',0),(25718,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Rohan\'s sending YOU to slay his druid? Very well.$B$BYou should know: Marl Wormthorn is as much demon as he is druid. Even a druid of his power doesn\'t have a chance against the demonic energies that run so deeply through this land. That does not, however, make him any less of an obstacle.',0),(25719,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Brilliantly done, $n. We have what we need to break the worgen\'s trance.',0),(25720,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hopefully, with this druid out of the picture, we can get back to our digging. The world is full of powerful artifacts, $n. You just need to be willing to do what it takes to get to them.$B$BFeel free to take one of these. The Reliquary is always happy to share some of its trove with fellow members of the Horde.',0),(25740,6,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Привет, $n! Я только тебя и жду.$B$BЧто, Омнурон назвал это \"разведывательной миссией\"? Ха! Лучший источник информации – трупы врагов.$B$BДавай-ка порезвимся!',19342),(25744,1,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'<Crazzle gets a gleam in his eye.>$B$BI\'ve got Kravel Koalbeard up there talking to one of their chiefs, but now that you\'re here, we\'ll have the rights to pump up their oil in no time!',19116),(25745,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Riznek gets a gleam in his eye.>$B$BI\'ve got Trackmaster Zherin up there talking to one of their chiefs, but now that you\'re here, we\'ll have the rights to pump up their oil in no time!',0),(25746,1,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Молодчина.$B$BТы прекрасно справляешься.',19342),(25747,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to see you again, $C. I almost thought we\'d lost you to the Wavespeaker\'s fool errand.$B$BDid anything come of it?',0),(25748,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'More naga are amassing to the south than reported too it seems. We shall have to move quickly then.',0),(25749,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are perhaps the most dependable person I\'ve ever met. I wish I could have more men half as thorough as you.',0),(25751,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are brave indeed! I\'ve seen you battling all manner of murloc, naga, and pointy-toothed fish, but that was nothing! The way you just sling those kelp bulbs under your arm like that is a whole new kind of fearless. BOOM! You could blow up at any second.$B$BYou\'re my kind of $R.',0),(25752,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did great up there! You devastated their ranks, but there were far more than we accounted for, and most of our men went down out there in the masses of naga.$B$BWe\'ll need to hold this position as long as possible to buy them time. Hopefully some of them will still make it to the rendezvous.',0),(25753,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you. Truly.$B$BWe need to get these men moving as soon as possible. I\'ll meet you back at the forward post soon, I\'m sure.',0),(25754,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Still so many? They must want something very important here to come in such numbers.$B$BI will be honest with you, $n, because you deserve at least that: I don\'t know how much hope there is. We will retreat shortly, but we won\'t be able to defend ourselves when they strike back. We don\'t have anywhere to run... we\'re running out of options.$B$BI\'m sorry, I should keep such thoughts to myself. Do me a favor and don\'t mention any of that to the men. I\'ll figure something out.',0),(25755,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re finished! Just in time. I don\'t think we could have held them much longer.$B$BAn artifact? Could this be something we can use against the naga? I suppose that would require finding it.$B$BWe may have to attend to more pressing matters first, until an opportunity to pursue this further presents itself.',0),(25756,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What?! How\'d they get that much gold to offer?$B$BWe don\'t have that kind of money!',19116),(25757,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What?! How\'d they get that much gold to offer?$B$BWe don\'t have that kind of money!',0),(25758,1,5,274,0,0,0,0,0,'Посмотри на них. Эти руны вызывают у меня резь в глазах. Вот эта вот призвана выжигать плоть? Неужели это правда? Ох! Погоди-ка...$B$BЭти пластины должны врезаться прямо в тело, вызывая адскую боль!',19342),(25759,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),(25760,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A Battlemaiden? I never heard of such a thing.$B$BThe way you explain it, it sounds like the naga forces are far greater in scope than the Admiral could possibly have realized. We might be able to learn more through the blade if we can find other locations where this Battlemaiden was present, but the information you gave me makes me fear for the admiral and his soldiers. We must warn them.',0),(25761,6,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ну и месиво, $n!$B$BТеперь на Хиджале стало одной заботой меньше.',19342),(25762,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did this favor to ingratiate yourself with me, but I will not sing your praises.$B$BI know what is to come. Where the sea failed, the great air spirit will strike you and your people down for your many transgressions against the elements.$B$BBegone from my sight!',19116),(25763,6,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Чем там они занимаются?$B$BЧто-то прячут? Так вот почему наши воздушные лазутчики не могут ничего разглядеть, несмотря на свое острое зрение.',19342),(25764,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Done, $n! Aviana’s egg will soon be delivered to the walls of the sanctuary. Do you think Aviana will return to us?',19342),(25770,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah! Nice to see those addlebrained mountaineers knew to hand the ale off to a real man to get the job done.$B$BWelcome to my survey. If you\'re of the mind to help Ironforge by takin\' over the intended jobs of some useless, lazy sods that call themselves dwarves, you\'re in the right place!',0),(25771,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just a shard?  Pfuh!  This gets me nothing!  Take your reward and get out of my sight.$B$BSounds familiar?  It should, because I say it a thousand times per day.$B$BOh how I loathe this world.\n',19116),(25772,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Simply amazing.  I had doubted that anyone could find another sphere, yet here it is, pulsating in my hands.$B$BWell done, $n!$B$BShould you find anymore--and I believe this to be an impossibility--return them to me and I shall reward you again.',19116),(25773,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, $n, this shard does explain the occurrence of the rift. The elemental planes have been in chaos in Outland ever since Draenor was destroyed. These shards cause a weakness in the already damaged elemental planes and allow the elementals to cross into our world$B$BWe\'re still looking into how these rifts are appearing in Azeroth. Keep bringing us the shards. Every shard we get brings us closer to understanding how these rifts are appearing.',0),(25774,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Genius! Now, where\'s that gold paint? I know it\'s around here somewhere.',19116),(25775,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Genius! Now, where\'s that gold paint? I know it\'s around here somewhere.',0),(25776,4,5,1,0,0,0,0,0,'С Сетрией покончено! Я знала, что стоило рискнуть.$B$BЯ пока побуду тут, должен же кто-то присмотреть за оставшимися в живых драконидами. А вот тебя уже ждут в святилище.',19342),(25778,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just put it down on the ground, $r.',19116),(25779,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just put it down on the ground, $R.',0),(25781,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),(25782,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions 